window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["ep-23.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">الشرح الأصلي بالإنكليزية.</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> ابحث بالرمز بخانة البحث. ابدأ دائماً بـ«الفحص المسبق» للمحرك قبل الرمز.</p><div class=\"ac-chips\"><span class=\"en-chip\">P = نقل الحركة: 62</span></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong>كيف تقرأ كود العطل</strong><small>الرقم بعد الشرطة يدل على نوع العطل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-legend\"><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-11</b><span>قصر على الأرضي</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-12</b><span>قصر على البطارية</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-13</b><span>دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-15</b><span>قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-16</b><span>الفولتية أقل من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-17</b><span>الفولتية أعلى من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-2A</b><span>مفتاح عالق Stuck</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-84 / 85</b><span>الإشارة أقل / أعلى من المدى</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-92</b><span>أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-00</b><span>عطل عام أو بدون نوع محدد</span></div></div><p class=\"bcm-note\">الحرف الأول: B = كهرباء الجسم · C = الهيكل والحساسات · P = نقل الحركة · U = اتصال الشبكة. نفّذ دائماً الفحص المسبق Pre-Diagnostic قبل خطوات أي كود.</p></div></details></div><input type=\"search\" class=\"ec-search acc-q\" placeholder=\"ابحث: كود العطل أو كلمة من الوصف\" aria-label=\"بحث\"><p class=\"bcm-note acc-cnt\">62 كود عطل. اضغط على الكود لترى شرحه.</p><div class=\"acc-list\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p0850 park/neutral switch performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P0850</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PARK/NEUTRAL SWITCH PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the engine running. Not equipped with a manual Transmission. No vehicle speed, TPS, MAP, BARO or 5-Volt reference DTCs active. Vehicle speed, engine speed and engine load calculations indicate that the vehicle is not in park or neutral.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) receives an invalid Park/Neutral switch state message for 0.32 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. If the vehicle is equipped with the stop/start feature, the system will be disabled when this DTC is active.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION RANGE SENSOR (TRS) WIRING ISSUES</li><li>COMMUNICATION FAILURE BETWEEN THE PCM AND THE TCM</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            This DTC could set during towing if the Manual Park Release Cable was not fully pulled and the pawl is in an intermediate position for too long.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and test drive the vehicle in accordance with the monitoring conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool read DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any CAN bus communication faults before continuing.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read TCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the TCM also have a DTC present for the Park/Neutral Switch or TRS Signal circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Transmission Control Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p0ea7 ltr pump performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P0EA7</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LTR PUMP PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the engine running. No active circuit faults for the Charge Air Cooler Pump Assembly. Charge Air Cooler Pump Assembly above a minimum calibrated threshold.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The PCM receives a LIN bus message from the Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump that the pump current is either much greater than, or less than expected at a particular rpm.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BLOCKAGE IN THE COOLANT FLOW</li><li>LOW COOLANT / NO COOLANT</li><li>EXCESSIVE AIR IS MIXED WITH THE COOLANT</li><li>CHARGE AIR COOLER COOLANT PUMP</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and test drive the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The vehicle must be driven in order to get the Charge Air Cooler Pump speed high enough for the diagnostic to run.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE CHARGE AIR COOLER COOLING SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for any of the following conditions, but not limited to: Low coolant / No coolant Blockage in the coolant flow Excessive air mixed with the coolant Charger Air Cooling system leaks Incorrect Charge Air Cooling system reservoir cap</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any issues found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate repairs.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1115 general temperature rationality\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1115</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">GENERAL TEMPERATURE RATIONALITY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Enable Conditions: Engine off time is greater than 480 minutes. Test conditions: The vehicle has been driven for one minute over 35 mph. Ambient temperature is greater than -64°C (-83°F).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The PCM compares the Ambient Air, Engine Coolant and Intake Air Temperature Sensor values. If the values of all the three sensors disagree with one another, a general</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">temperature sensor irrationality is declared.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>EXCESSIVE RESISTANCE IN THE SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT</li><li>EXCESSIVE RESISTANCE IN THE SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT</li><li>SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT</li><li>TEMPERATURE SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If possible, allow the vehicle to sit with the ignition off for more than 480 minutes in an environment where the temperature is consistent and above -7°C (19.4°F).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Test drive the vehicle. The vehicle must exceed 48 km/h (30 mph) during the test drive. Do not cycle the ignition off when the test drive is completed.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           All ECT, Intake Air and Ambient Air Temperature Sensor codes must be diagnosed and repaired before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           In cold weather, this DTC could be set by a block heater and no repair would be required.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>TEMPERATURE SENSOR CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the ECT, Ambient Air Temp and Intake Air Temp Sensor temp values.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Allow the engine to reach normal operating temperature while monitoring the three Sensor temperature values.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the temperature for each of the Sensors increasing properly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>TEMPERATURE SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the suspected sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read the voltage of the suspected Sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect a jumper between the Sensor Signal circuit and the Sensor ground circuit of the ECT Sensor, IAT Sensor and AAT Sensor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the voltage reading start at 4.8 to 5.0 volts and decrease to 0 volts when the jumper was installed?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Sensor and Control Module connectors. If OK, replace the appropriate Temperature Sensor. Refer to SENSOR, COOLANT TEMPERATURE, REMOVAL . Or refer to SENSOR, AIR TEMPERATURE, INLET, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Remove the jumper before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>EXCESSIVE RESISTANCE IN A TEMPERATURE SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the BCM C4 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the Sensor Signal circuit from the Sensor harness connector to the appropriate terminal of PCM C2 harness connector for the ECT Sensor and IAT Sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (G31) AAT Sensor Signal circuit from the Sensor harness connector to the BCM C4 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the excessive resistance in the Temperature Sensor Signal circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>EXCESSIVE RESISTANCE IN A SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (K900) Sensor ground circuit from the ECT Sensor and IAT Sensor to the appropriate terminal of PCM harness</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (G931) Sensor ground circuit from the AAT Sensor harness connector to the BCM C4 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the excessive resistance in the Sensor ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the related Sensors and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the related Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1128 closed loop fueling not achieved - bank 1 upstream\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1128</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CLOSED LOOP FUELING NOT ACHIEVED - BANK 1 UPSTREAM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">With the engine running in closed loop mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The O2 Sensor has not been in closed loop control at least once on each of the two consecutive trips.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RESTRICTED FUEL SUPPLY LINE</li><li>FUEL PUMP INLET STRAINER PLUGGED</li><li>FUEL PUMP MODULE</li><li>O2 SIGNAL CIRCUIT</li><li>O2 RETURN CIRCUIT</li><li>O2 SENSOR</li><li>MAP SENSOR</li><li>ECT SENSOR</li><li>ENGINE MECHANICAL PROBLEM</li><li>FUEL FILTER/PRESSURE REGULATOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>ECT SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any other O2 Sensor DTCs that are present before continuing with this test procedure.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This test works best if performed on a cold engine (cold soak).</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Engine Coolant Temperature (ECT) Sensor value. If the engine was allowed to sit overnight (cold soak), the temperature value should be a sensible value that is somewhere close to the ambient temperature.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Compare the ECT Sensor value with the IAT Sensor and AAT Sensor values.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If engine coolant temperature is above 82°C (180°F), allow the engine to cool until 65°C (150°F) is reached.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>During engine warm-up, monitor the ECT Sensor value. The temperature value change should be a smooth transition from start up to normal operating temperature 82°C (180°F). The value should reach at least 82°C (180°F).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the ECT Sensor value within a reasonable range with the other sensors at ignition on and did the ECT value increase smoothly and did it reach at least 82°C (180°F)?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If OK, replace the Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           It may be necessary to drive the vehicle to meet the conditions to set this DTC, try to repeat the conditions in which the fault originally set by reviewing the Freeze Frame data.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>O2 SENSOR HEATER OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Wait a minimum of 10 minutes to allow the O2 Sensor to cool down before continuing the test. Allow the O2 Sensor voltage to stabilize at 5.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, actuate the O2 Sensor 1/1 Heater Test.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, monitor O2 Sensor 1/1 voltage for at least two minutes.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the voltage stay above 4.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the O2 Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If no problems are found, replace the O2 Sensor.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>O2 SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, monitor the O2 Sensor 1/1 reading.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage switching between 2.5 and 3.4 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Check the O2 Sensor terminals for pushed out, corroded or spread terminals and verify that the wires for the O2 Sensor are not open or shorted to ground. If no problems are found, replace the O2 Sensor.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>MAP SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect a Vacuum Gauge to a Manifold Vacuum source.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Allow the engine to idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If engine will not idle, maintain a constant rpm above idle.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the MAP Sensor vacuum value.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the scan tool reading within one inch of Hg as compared to the Vacuum Gauge reading?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the MAP Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If OK, replace the MAP Sensor.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform the CHECKING THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM test procedure. Refer to CHECKING THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM (HARD START) .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>ENGINE MECHANICAL PROBLEM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for any of the following conditions/mechanical problems: AIR INDUCTION SYSTEM - must be free from leaks ENGINE VACUUM - must be at least 13 inches in neutral ENGINE VALVE TIMING - must be within specifications ENGINE COMPRESSION - must be within specifications ENGINE EXHAUST SYSTEM - must be free of any restrictions or leaks ENGINE PCV SYSTEM - must flow freely TORQUE CONVERTER STALL SPEED - must be within specifications POWER BRAKE BOOSTER - no internal vacuum leaks FUEL - must be free of contamination FUEL INJECTOR - plugged or restricted injector, control wire not connected to correct injector</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any engine mechanical problems?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the related Sensor and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the related Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1129 closed loop fueling not achieved - bank 2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1129</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CLOSED LOOP FUELING NOT ACHIEVED - BANK 2</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">With the engine running in closed loop mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The O2 Sensor has not been in closed loop control at least once on each of the two consecutive trips.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RESTRICTED FUEL SUPPLY LINE</li><li>FUEL PUMP INLET STRAINER PLUGGED</li><li>FUEL PUMP MODULE</li><li>O2 SIGNAL CIRCUIT</li><li>O2 RETURN CIRCUIT</li><li>O2 SENSOR</li><li>MAP SENSOR</li><li>ECT SENSOR</li><li>ENGINE MECHANICAL PROBLEM</li><li>FUEL FILTER/PRESSURE REGULATOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>ECT SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          For this test to be valid, the thermostat must be operating correctly.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          This test works best if performed on a cold engine (cold soak).</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Engine Coolant Temperature (ECT) Sensor value. If the engine was allowed to sit overnight (cold soak), the temperature value should be a sensible value that is somewhere close to the ambient temperature.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If engine coolant temperature is above 82°C (180°F), allow the engine to cool until 65°C (150°F) is reached.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the Engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>During engine warm-up, monitor the ECT Sensor value. The temperature value change should be a smooth transition from start up to normal operating temperature 82°C (180°F). The value should reach at least 82°C (180°F).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the ECT value increase smoothly and did it reach at least 82°C (180°F)?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If OK, replace the Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Diagnose all other DTCs before continuing.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           It may be necessary to drive the vehicle to meet the conditions to set this DTC, try to repeat the conditions in which the fault originally set by reviewing the Freeze Frame data.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>O2 SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform the CHECKING THE OXYGEN SENSOR OPERATION test procedure. Refer to CHECKING THE OXYGEN SENSOR OPERATION .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Were any problems found with the O2 Sensors?</span></div><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>MAP SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform the CHECKING THE MAP SENSOR OPERATION test procedure. Refer to CHECKING THE MAP SENSOR OPERATION .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found with the MAP Sensor?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECKING FUEL PRESSURE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform the CHECKING THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM test procedure. Refer to CHECKING THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM (HARD START) .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found with the fuel system?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>ENGINE MECHANICAL PROBLEM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for any of the following conditions/mechanical problems: AIR INDUCTION SYSTEM - must be free from leaks ENGINE VACUUM - must be at least 13 inches in neutral ENGINE VALVE TIMING - must be within specifications ENGINE COMPRESSION - must be within specifications ENGINE EXHAUST SYSTEM - must be free of any restrictions or leaks ENGINE PCV SYSTEM - must flow freely TORQUE CONVERTER STALL SPEED - must be within specifications POWER BRAKE BOOSTER - no internal vacuum leaks FUEL - must be free of contamination FUEL INJECTOR - plugged or restricted injector, control wire not connected to correct injector</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any engine mechanical problems?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the related Sensor and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the related Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p112a o2 sensor 1/1 pumping undercurrent\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P112A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 SENSOR 1/1 PUMPING UNDERCURRENT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The wide-band O2 Sensor operates differently than traditional O2 Sensors. The wide-band O2 Sensor tip consists of two cells that provide different functions, a measurement chamber and a detection chamber with pumping capabilities. The oxygen pumping function is the ability to pump oxygen into or out of the measurement chamber depending on the level of oxygen in the measurement chamber. This function provides the wide-band sensing capabilities and is critical for proper oxygen measurement. The O2 Sensor Reference circuit provides a common bias supply to both the O2 Sensor Signal and the O2 Sensor Pump Cell Current circuits.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">During normal operation, the O2 Sensor Reference voltage and O2 Sensor Signal voltage will be a fixed voltage value. The O2 Sensor Current Pump voltage will switch from between 0.45 volts above and below the fixed O2 Sensor Return voltage, allowing current to flow in either direction through the pump. This correlates with the pumping of oxygen into and out of the measurement chamber. On a properly operating vehicle, this happens very quickly and the voltage reading should maintain a steady 0.45 volts when</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">taking a voltage measurement between the O2 Sensor Signal circuit and the O2 Sensor Reference circuit of the O2 Sensor with the engine running and the O2 Sensor operating in closed loop.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the exhaust stream has a lean air/fuel ratio (high oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward +0.45 volts pumping oxygen out of the measurement chamber. When the exhaust stream has a rich air/fuel ratio (relatively low oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward -0.45 volts pumping oxygen into the measurement chamber.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously with the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) detects an undercurrent condition on the internal driver for the O2 Sensor 1/1 Pump Current circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FAULTY O2 SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR OTHER DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Refer to the recorded DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any other Upstream O2 Sensor DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the applicable diagnostic procedure(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>REPLACE THE O2 SENSOR AND RETEST FOR DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the O2 Sensor in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the O2 Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, erase all DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition off for a minimum of 10.0 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Using the When Monitored and Set Conditions above and recorded data, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replacing the faulty O2 Sensor repaired the fault.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the poor connections.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p112b o2 sensor 1/1 pumping overcurrent\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P112B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 SENSOR 1/1 PUMPING OVERCURRENT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The wide-band O2 Sensor operates differently than traditional O2 Sensors. The wide-band O2 Sensor tip consists of two cells that provide different functions, a measurement chamber and a detection chamber with pumping capabilities. The oxygen pumping function is the ability to pump oxygen into or out of the measurement chamber depending on the level of oxygen in the measurement chamber. This function provides the wide-band sensing capabilities and is critical for proper oxygen measurement. The O2 Sensor Reference circuit provides a common bias supply to both the O2 Sensor Signal and the O2 Sensor Pump Cell Current circuits.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">During normal operation, the O2 Sensor Reference voltage and O2 Sensor Signal voltage will be a fixed voltage value. The O2 Sensor Current Pump voltage will switch from between 0.45 volts above and below the fixed O2 Sensor Return voltage, allowing current to flow in either direction through the pump. This correlates with the pumping of oxygen into and out of the measurement chamber. On a properly operating vehicle, this happens very quickly and the voltage reading should maintain a steady 0.45 volts when</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">taking a voltage measurement between the O2 Sensor Signal circuit and the O2 Sensor Reference circuit of the O2 Sensor with the engine running and the O2 Sensor operating in closed loop.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the exhaust stream has a lean air/fuel ratio (high oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward +0.45 volts pumping oxygen out of the measurement chamber. When the exhaust stream has a rich air/fuel ratio (relatively low oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward -0.45 volts pumping oxygen into the measurement chamber.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously with the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) detects an overcurrent condition on the internal driver for the O2 Sensor 1/1 Pump Current circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FAULTY O2 SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR OTHER DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Refer to the recorded DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any other Upstream O2 Sensor DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the applicable diagnostic procedure(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>REPLACE THE O2 SENSOR AND RETEST FOR DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the O2 Sensor in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the O2 Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, erase all DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition off for a minimum of 10.0 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Using the When Monitored and Set Conditions above and recorded data, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replacing the faulty O2 Sensor repaired the fault.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the poor connections.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p112c o2 sensor 2/1 pumping undercurrent\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P112C</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 SENSOR 2/1 PUMPING UNDERCURRENT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The wide-band O2 Sensor operates differently than traditional O2 Sensors. The wide-band O2 Sensor tip consists of two cells that provide different functions, a measurement chamber and a detection chamber with pumping capabilities. The oxygen pumping function is the ability to pump oxygen into or out of the measurement chamber depending on the level of oxygen in the measurement chamber. This function provides the wide-band sensing capabilities and is critical for proper oxygen measurement. The O2 Sensor Reference circuit provides a common bias supply to both the O2 Sensor Signal and the O2 Sensor Pump Cell Current circuits.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">During normal operation, the O2 Sensor Reference voltage and O2 Sensor Signal voltage will be a fixed voltage value. The O2 Sensor Current Pump voltage will switch from between 0.45 volts above and below the fixed O2 Sensor Return voltage, allowing current to flow in either direction through the pump. This correlates with the pumping of oxygen into and out of the measurement chamber. On a properly operating vehicle, this happens very quickly and the voltage reading should maintain a steady 0.45 volts when</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">taking a voltage measurement between the O2 Sensor Signal circuit and the O2 Sensor Reference circuit of the O2 Sensor with the engine running and the O2 Sensor operating in closed loop.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the exhaust stream has a lean air/fuel ratio (high oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward +0.45 volts pumping oxygen out of the measurement chamber. When the exhaust stream has a rich air/fuel ratio (relatively low oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward -0.45 volts pumping oxygen into the measurement chamber.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously with the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) detects an undercurrent condition on the internal driver for the O2 Sensor 1/1 Pump Current circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FAULTY O2 SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR OTHER DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Refer to the recorded DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any other Upstream O2 Sensor DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the applicable diagnostic procedure(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>REPLACE THE O2 SENSOR 2/1 AND RETEST FOR DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the O2 Sensor 2/1 in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the O2 Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, erase all DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition off for a minimum of 10.0 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Using the When Monitored and Set Conditions above and recorded data, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replacing the faulty O2 Sensor repaired the fault.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the poor connections.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p112d o2 sensor 2/1 pumping overcurrent\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P112D</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 SENSOR 2/1 PUMPING OVERCURRENT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The wide-band O2 Sensor operates differently than traditional O2 Sensors. The wide-band O2 Sensor tip consists of two cells that provide different functions, a measurement chamber and a detection chamber with pumping capabilities. The oxygen pumping function is the ability to pump oxygen into or out of the measurement chamber depending on the level of oxygen in the measurement chamber. This function provides the wide-band sensing capabilities and is critical for proper oxygen measurement. The O2 Sensor Reference circuit provides a common bias supply to both the O2 Sensor Signal and the O2 Sensor Pump Cell Current circuits.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">During normal operation, the O2 Sensor Reference voltage and O2 Sensor Signal voltage will be a fixed voltage value. The O2 Sensor Current Pump voltage will switch from between 0.45 volts above and below the fixed O2 Sensor Return voltage, allowing current to flow in either direction through the pump. This correlates with the pumping of oxygen into and out of the measurement chamber. On a properly operating vehicle, this happens very quickly and the voltage reading should maintain a steady 0.45 volts when</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">taking a voltage measurement between the O2 Sensor Signal circuit and the O2 Sensor Reference circuit of the O2 Sensor with the engine running and the O2 Sensor operating in closed loop.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the exhaust stream has a lean air/fuel ratio (high oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward +0.45 volts pumping oxygen out of the measurement chamber. When the exhaust stream has a rich air/fuel ratio (relatively low oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward -0.45 volts pumping oxygen into the measurement chamber.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously with the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) detects an overcurrent condition on the internal driver for the O2 Sensor 2/1 Pump Current circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FAULTY O2 SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR OTHER DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Refer to the recorded DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any other Upstream O2 Sensor DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the applicable diagnostic procedure(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>REPLACE THE O2 SENSOR 2/1 AND RETEST FOR DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the O2 Sensor 2/1 in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the O2 Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, erase all DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition off for a minimum of 10.0 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Using the When Monitored and Set Conditions above and recorded data, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replacing the faulty O2 Sensor repaired the fault.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the poor connections.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p112e o2 sensor 1/1 performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P112E</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 SENSOR 1/1 PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The wide-band O2 Sensor operates differently than traditional O2 Sensors. The wide-band O2 Sensor tip consists of two cells that provide different functions, a measurement chamber and a detection chamber with pumping capabilities. The oxygen pumping function is the ability to pump oxygen into or out of the measurement chamber depending on the level of oxygen in the measurement chamber. This function provides the wide-band sensing capabilities and is critical for proper oxygen measurement. The O2 Sensor Reference circuit provides a common bias supply to both the O2 Sensor Signal and the O2 Sensor Pump Cell Current circuits.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">During normal operation, the O2 Sensor Reference voltage and O2 Sensor Signal voltage will be a fixed voltage value. The O2 Sensor Current Pump voltage will switch from between 0.45 volts above and below the fixed O2 Sensor Return voltage, allowing current to flow in either direction through the pump. This correlates with the pumping of oxygen into and out of the measurement chamber. On a properly operating vehicle, this happens very quickly and the voltage reading should maintain a steady 0.45 volts when</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">taking a voltage measurement between the O2 Sensor Signal circuit and the O2 Sensor Reference circuit of the O2 Sensor with the engine running and the O2 Sensor operating in closed loop.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the exhaust stream has a lean air/fuel ratio (high oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward +0.45 volts pumping oxygen out of the measurement chamber. When the exhaust stream has a rich air/fuel ratio (relatively low oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward -0.45 volts pumping oxygen into the measurement chamber.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously with the engine running above 300 rpm.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) detects an internal hardware failure on the Pump Cell ASIC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FAULTY O2 SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR OTHER DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Refer to the recorded DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any other Upstream O2 Sensor DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the applicable diagnostic procedure(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>REPLACE THE O2 SENSOR 1/1 AND RETEST FOR DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the O2 Sensor in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the O2 Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, erase all DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition off for a minimum of 10.0 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Using the When Monitored and Set Conditions above and recorded data, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replacing the faulty O2 Sensor repaired the fault.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the poor connections.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p112f o2 sensor 2/1 performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P112F</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 SENSOR 2/1 PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The wide-band O2 Sensor operates differently than traditional O2 Sensors. The wide-band O2 Sensor tip consists of two cells that provide different functions, a measurement chamber and a detection chamber with pumping capabilities. The oxygen pumping function is the ability to pump oxygen into or out of the measurement chamber depending on the level of oxygen in the measurement chamber. This function provides the wide-band sensing capabilities and is critical for proper oxygen measurement. The O2 Sensor Reference circuit provides a common bias supply to both the O2 Sensor Signal and the O2 Sensor Pump Cell Current circuits.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">During normal operation, the O2 Sensor Reference voltage and O2 Sensor Signal voltage will be a fixed voltage value. The O2 Sensor Current Pump voltage will switch from between 0.45 volts above and below the fixed O2 Sensor Return voltage, allowing current to flow in either direction through the pump. This correlates with the pumping of oxygen into and out of the measurement chamber. On a properly operating vehicle, this happens very quickly and the voltage reading should maintain a steady 0.45 volts when</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">taking a voltage measurement between the O2 Sensor Signal circuit and the O2 Sensor Reference circuit of the O2 Sensor with the engine running and the O2 Sensor operating in closed loop.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the exhaust stream has a lean air/fuel ratio (high oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward +0.45 volts pumping oxygen out of the measurement chamber. When the exhaust stream has a rich air/fuel ratio (relatively low oxygen content) the pumping element voltage will move toward -0.45 volts pumping oxygen into the measurement chamber.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously with the engine running above 300 rpm.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) detects an internal hardware failure on the Pump Cell ASIC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FAULTY O2 SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR OTHER DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Refer to the recorded DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any other Upstream O2 Sensor DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the applicable diagnostic procedure(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>REPLACE THE O2 SENSOR AND RETEST FOR DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the O2 Sensor in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the O2 Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, erase all DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition off for a minimum of 10.0 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Using the When Monitored and Set Conditions above and recorded data, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replacing the faulty O2 Sensor repaired the fault.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the poor connections.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p113d o2 sensor 1/1 slow response (high frequency)\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P113D</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 SENSOR 1/1 SLOW RESPONSE (HIGH FREQUENCY)</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For an aged Upstream Oxygen (O2) Sensor, the response rate to the air/fuel change is slower than when it was new. The O2 Sensor tends to move less with the same air/fuel changes in a given time frame. Therefore by observing the activity of voltage readings from the Upstream O2 Sensor, the quality of the O2 Sensor can be detected. The Downstream O2 Sensor is located in the exhaust path behind the Catalytic Converter, and is monitored for proper response to assure optimum Catalytic Converter efficiency. The Downstream O2 Sensor response monitor is intended to diagnose a Downstream O2 Sensor that is not moving or stuck in a voltage window and to insure accurate information for catalyst monitor diagnosis.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine speed between 1000 and 2750 rpm. Minimum engine run time of 20 seconds. The ECT Sensor temperature at least 60°C (140°F). MAP Sensor reading is between 21 - 96 kPa (6.2 - 28.3 in Hg).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Oxygen Sensor signal does not switch adequately at high frequency.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>EXHAUST LEAK</li><li>O2 SENSOR 1/1 SIGNAL CIRCUIT</li><li>O2 SENSOR 1/1 RETURN CIRCUIT</li><li>O2 SENSOR 1/1</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check for contaminants that may have damaged the O2 Sensor: contaminated fuel, unapproved silicone, oil and coolant.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          After any repairs have been made, verify proper O2 Sensor operation. If all the O2 Sensor voltage readings have not returned to normal, follow the diagnostic procedure for the remaining O2 Sensors.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Allow the engine to reach normal operating temperature.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          It may be necessary to drive the vehicle to meet the conditions to set this DTC, try to repeat the conditions in which the fault originally set by reviewing the Freeze Frame data.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECKING THE EXHAUST SYSTEM FOR LEAKS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform the CHECKING THE EXHAUST SYSTEM FOR LEAKS diagnostic procedure. Refer to CHECKING THE EXHAUST SYSTEM FOR LEAKS .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (K41) O2 SENSOR 1/1 SIGNAL CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the O2 Sensor 1/1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (K41) O2 Sensor 1/1 Signal circuit in the O2 Sensor 1/1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage between 4.1 and 5.0 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Check the (K41) O2 Sensor 1/1 Signal circuit for a short to ground, open, or short to voltage. If OK, replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (K902) O2 SENSOR 1/1 RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (K902) O2 Sensor 1/1 Return circuit in the O2 Sensor 1/1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage at 2.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Check the (K902) O2 Sensor 1/1 Return circuit for a short to ground, open, or short to voltage. If OK, replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>O2 SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for signs of contaminants that may have damaged the O2 Sensor, such as contaminated fuel, unapproved silicone, oil and coolant.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the O2 Sensor 1/1 and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM). Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires. Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the O2 Sensor 1/1 and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Oxygen Sensor 1/1 in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, OXYGEN, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p113e o2 sensor 2/1 slow response (high frequency)\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P113E</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 SENSOR 2/1 SLOW RESPONSE (HIGH FREQUENCY)</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For an aged Upstream Oxygen (O2) Sensor, the response rate to the air/fuel change is slower than when it was new. The O2 Sensor tends to move less with the same air/fuel changes in a given time frame. Therefore by observing the activity of voltage readings from the Upstream O2 Sensor, the quality of the O2 Sensor can be detected. The Downstream O2 Sensor is located in the exhaust path behind the Catalytic Converter, and is monitored for proper response to assure optimum Catalytic Converter efficiency. The Downstream O2 Sensor response monitor is intended to diagnose a Downstream O2 Sensor that is not moving or stuck in a voltage window and to insure accurate information for catalyst monitor diagnosis.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ECT Sensor above 60°C (140°F). Minimum engine run time of 20 seconds. engine speed between 1000 and 2750 rpm. MAP reading is between 21 - 96 Kpa (6.2 - 28.3 in Hg).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Oxygen Sensor signal does not switch adequately at high frequency.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>EXHAUST LEAK</li><li>O2 SENSOR 2/1 SIGNAL CIRCUIT</li><li>O2 SENSOR 2/1 RETURN CIRCUIT</li><li>O2 SENSOR 2/1</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for contaminants that may have damaged the O2 Sensor: contaminated fuel, unapproved silicone, oil and coolant.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           After the repairs have been made, verify proper O2 Sensor operation. If all the O2 Sensor voltage readings have not returned to normal, follow the diagnostic procedure for the remaining O2 Sensors.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Allow the engine to reach normal operating temperature.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           It may be necessary to drive the vehicle to meet the conditions to set this DTC, try to repeat the conditions in which the fault originally set by reviewing the Freeze Frame data.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECKING THE EXHAUST SYSTEM FOR LEAKS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform the CHECKING THE EXHAUST SYSTEM FOR LEAKS diagnostic procedure. Refer to CHECKING THE EXHAUST SYSTEM FOR LEAKS .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (K43) O2 SENSOR 2/1 SIGNAL CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the O2 Sensor 2/1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition ON.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (K43) O2 Sensor 2/1 Signal circuit in the O2 Sensor 2/1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage between 4.1 and 5.0 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Check the (K43) O2 Sensor 2/1 Signal circuit for a short to ground, open or short to voltage. If OK, replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (K906) O2 SENSOR 2/1 RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (K906) O2 Sensor 2/1 Return circuit in the O2 Sensor 2/1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage at 2.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Check the (K906) O2 Sensor 2/1 Return circuit for a short to ground, open or short to voltage. If OK, replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>OXYGEN SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for signs of contaminants that may have damaged the O2 Sensor, such as contaminated fuel, unapproved silicone, oil and coolant.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the Oxygen Sensor 2/1 and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM). Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires. Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the O2 Sensor 2/1 and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Oxygen Sensor 2/1 in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1205 fuel pump control module internal performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1205</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">FUEL PUMP CONTROL MODULE INTERNAL PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">GENERAL OPERATION: When the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) receives a &#x27;Start&#x27; or &#x27;Run&#x27; signal, it energizes the Fuel Pump Relay which sends a continuous 12.0 volt supply to the Fuel Pump Control Module (FPCM). Depending on vehicle configuration, the Fuel Pump Relay can be either a removable component or be part of the Printed Circuit Board inside the Power Distribution Center (PDC) and not separately replaceable. The PCM sends commands to the FPCM through a Pulse Width Modulated</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">(PWM) control signal. The FPCM in turn regulates the PWM voltage output to the Fuel Pump Assembly based on inputs from the Fuel Rail Pressure (FRP) Sensor and other engine demands. The PWM signal will vary from 10-100% to maintain the proper fuel pressure in the system. This is a Constant Pressure Fuel system which means any fuel pressure test performed on the Fuel Pump should show a continuous pressure (regardless of the changes in PWM).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">DIAGNOSTICS: The PCM directly monitors the Fuel Pump Relay Control circuit and the FRP Sensor for circuit faults. The PCM also monitors the feedback from the FRP Sensor to determine if the Fuel Pump Assembly is able to achieve and maintain the desired pressure in the fuel system. The FPCM is a smart device which monitors the Fuel Pump Assembly wiring for circuit faults and reports the faults to the PCM. The PCM receives the feedback from the FPCM through the PWM feedback signal. These faults reported will be stored in the PCM. The pump motor is also monitored for mechanical and performance issues such as Fuel Pump Motor over temperature, blocked pump rotor, dry run, and pump motor speed deviation. If any of these conditions are present, the FPCM will default the duty cycle for the Fuel Pump Assembly to (80%) to maintain fuel pressure. The default duty cycle could cause the fuel system pressure to be higher than the typical 58.0 psi, which can cause the P062A Fuel Pump Control Performance fault to set.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         The P062A DTC will occur if the fuel pressure is too high or too low in the system. The Fuel Pump Assembly can be failing and still produce high fuel pressure in the system when the FPCM is defaulted to 80% duty cycle. Therefore, if this DTC is not accompanied by another fuel control system DTC, and the Fuel Rail Pressure Sensor is reading correctly, the Fuel Pump Assembly is the most likely cause of this DTC.</div></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the engine running Battery voltage greater than 11.0 volts</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Fuel Pump Control Module (FPCM) loses the ability to detect short circuits, output state, over voltage, and thermal runaway. When this DTC is set; The FPCM will continue to run the Fuel Pump Module in the normal mode at the duty cycle commanded by the PCM. This is an internal FPCM fault.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">MIL is illuminated on the second consecutive trip that the diagnostic fails. The MIL will be turned off on the third consecutive trip that the diagnostic passes.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FUEL PUMP CONTROL MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on, engine not running.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Fuel Pump Control Module in accordance with the service information. Refer to MODULE, FUEL PUMP CONTROL, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1206 fuel pump control module open circuit to fuel pump\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1206</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">FUEL PUMP CONTROL MODULE OPEN CIRCUIT TO FUEL PUMP</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">GENERAL OPERATION: When the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) receives a &#x27;Start&#x27; or &#x27;Run&#x27; signal, it energizes the Fuel Pump Relay which sends a continuous 12.0 volt supply to the Fuel Pump Control Module (FPCM). Depending on vehicle configuration, the Fuel Pump Relay can be either a removable component or be part of the Printed Circuit Board inside the Power Distribution Center (PDC) and not separately replaceable. The PCM sends commands to the FPCM through a Pulse Width Modulated</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">(PWM) control signal. The FPCM in turn regulates the PWM voltage output to the Fuel Pump Assembly based on inputs from the Fuel Rail Pressure (FRP) Sensor and other engine demands. The PWM signal will vary from 10-100% to maintain the proper fuel pressure in the system. This is a Constant Pressure Fuel system which means any fuel pressure test performed on the Fuel Pump should show a continuous pressure (regardless of the changes in PWM).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">DIAGNOSTICS: The PCM directly monitors the Fuel Pump Relay Control circuit and the FRP Sensor for circuit faults. The PCM also monitors the feedback from the FRP Sensor to determine if the Fuel Pump Assembly is able to achieve and maintain the desired pressure in the fuel system. The FPCM is a smart device which monitors the Fuel Pump Assembly wiring for circuit faults and reports the faults to the PCM. The PCM receives the feedback from the FPCM through the PWM feedback signal. These faults reported will be stored in the PCM. The pump motor is also monitored for mechanical and performance issues such as Fuel Pump Motor over temperature, blocked pump rotor, dry run, and pump motor speed deviation. If any of these conditions are present, the FPCM will default the duty cycle for the Fuel Pump Assembly to (80%) to maintain fuel pressure. The default duty cycle could cause the fuel system pressure to be higher than the typical 58.0 psi, which can cause the P062A Fuel Pump Control Performance fault to set.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The P062A DTC will occur if the fuel pressure is too high or too low in the system. The Fuel Pump Assembly can be failing and still produce high fuel pressure in the system when the FPCM is defaulted to 80% duty cycle. Therefore, if this DTC is not accompanied by another fuel control system DTC, and the Fuel Rail Pressure Sensor is reading correctly, the Fuel Pump Assembly is the most likely cause of this DTC.</div></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on Battery voltage greater than 10.4 volts. The FPCM is powered on. The ASD Relay is energized. The Fuel Pump Relay is energized.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The FPCM detects an open circuit or high resistance on Pulse Width Modulated (PWM) Fuel Pump Control circuit to the Fuel Pump assembly.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">MIL is illuminated on the second consecutive trip that the diagnostic fails. The MIL will be turned off on the third consecutive trip that the diagnostic passes.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FPCM PUMP CONTROL CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>FPCM PUMP RETURN CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>FUEL PUMP ASSEMBLY</li><li>FUEL PUMP CONTROL MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>READ AND RECORD DTCS AND ENVIRONMENTAL DATA - ERASE DTCS AND CHECK FOR THE DTC TO RETURN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in all Electronic Control Units (ECUs) and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>For future reference, with the scan tool, run and save a vehicle Scan Report and all related recorded data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase all DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition off for a minimum of 10.0 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Using the When Monitored and Set Conditions above and recorded data, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (N13) FUEL PUMP PWM CONTROL CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the FPCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Fuel Pump Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (N13) Fuel Pump PWM Control circuit between the FPCM harness connector and the Fuel Pump assembly harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (N13) Fuel Pump PWM Control circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (N14) FUEL PUMP PWM RETURN CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (N14) Fuel Pump PWM Return circuit between the FPCM harness connector and the Fuel Pump assembly harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (N14) Fuel Pump PWM Return circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>REPLACE THE FUEL PUMP ASSEMBLY AND RETEST FOR DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the Fuel Pump Assembly in accordance with the Service Information. (Refer to 14 - Fuel System/Fuel Delivery, Auxiliary/PUMP, Fuel, Auxiliary/Removal).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the Fuel Pump Assembly and PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Using the recorded Freeze Frame and the When Monitored conditions, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Fuel Pump Control Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replacing the Fuel Pump Assembly repaired the fault.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1214 active exhaust valve 1 circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1214</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the Active Exhaust Valves are to reduce exhaust noise in order to meet pass-by noise regulations. The Active Exhaust Valves consist of two parts. First is the mechanical butterfly valves that are welded into the exhaust pipe on each bank. Mounted to each of these is a smart actuator. They are connected to the mechanical valves through a transmission spring. This is to help reduce heat from transferring between the mechanical butterfly valves and the actuators.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Active Exhaust Valve actuators communicate with the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) over a LIN Bus circuit. The Active Exhaust Valve actuator 1 (left) and Active Exhaust Valve actuator 2 (right) each has a unique part number/internal ID. The PCM can identify each actuator location by this unique ID. The PCM sends a position command to the Active Exhaust Valve actuators based on engine torque, rpm and vehicle speed. The Active Exhaust Valve actuators move the butterfly valves to the commanded position. An internal Hall Effect sensor counts the pulses and determines valve position. The valve actuators are calibrated at every Key-ON event. The PCM sends full open and full closed commands and checks actual position against commanded position. If for any reason the calibration is unsuccessful, the actuators are self-diagnosing and report fault flags to the PCM over the LIN Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the valve position doesn&#x27;t match a predetermined calibration, a performance code is set and the valves will default to the full open position. If an actuator is not attached to the mechanical valve, or the transmission spring is broken or missing, the actuator will continue to rotate indefinitely and set a fault. Also, if the mechanical valve is stuck and will not move, a fault will set.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           There is a crossover in the exhaust, upstream of the valves that will allow the exhaust to flow through the open valve in the event one of the valves is stuck closed.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the transmission spring breaks or the valve becomes disconnected from the actuator for whatever reason the valve assembly likely will cause a rattling noise with the engine running.</div></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs with the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The LIN communication device in the Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator reports an open circuit to the PCM.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator defaults to open position.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 ACTUATOR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 ACTUATOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check connections to Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact at the Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator and PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Replace the Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 1</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1215 active exhaust valve 1 circuit low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1215</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 CIRCUIT LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the Active Exhaust Valves are to reduce exhaust noise in order to meet pass-by noise regulations. The Active Exhaust Valves consist of two parts. First is the mechanical butterfly valves that are welded into the exhaust pipe on each bank. Mounted to each of these is a smart actuator. They are connected to the mechanical valves through a transmission spring. This is to help reduce heat from transferring between the mechanical butterfly valves and the actuators.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Active Exhaust Valve actuators communicate with the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) over a LIN Bus circuit. The Active Exhaust Valve actuator 1 (left) and Active Exhaust Valve actuator 2 (right) each has a unique part number/internal ID. The PCM can identify each actuator location by this unique ID. The PCM sends a position command to the Active Exhaust Valve actuators based on engine torque, rpm and vehicle speed. The Active Exhaust Valve actuators move the butterfly valves to the commanded position. An internal Hall Effect sensor counts the pulses and determines valve position. The valve actuators are calibrated at every Key-ON event. The PCM sends full open and full closed commands and checks actual position against commanded position. If for any reason the calibration is unsuccessful, the actuators are self-diagnosing and report fault flags to the PCM over the LIN Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the valve position doesn&#x27;t match a predetermined calibration, a performance code is set and the valves will default to the full open position. If an actuator is not attached to the mechanical valve, or the transmission spring is broken or missing, the actuator will continue to rotate indefinitely and set a fault. Also, if the mechanical valve is stuck and will not move, a fault will set.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           There is a crossover in the exhaust, upstream of the valves that will allow the exhaust to flow through the open valve in the event one of the valves is stuck closed.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the transmission spring breaks or the valve becomes disconnected from the actuator for whatever reason the valve assembly likely will cause a rattling noise with the engine running.</div></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs with the engine running.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The PCM detects that the Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator Fused B+ circuit voltage is below 8.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FUSED B+ CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 ACTUATOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:           When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan. Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Start the engine.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Allow the engine to idle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F929) FUSED B+ CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Before continuing to the next step, confirm that the AEV 1 Actuator harness connector was properly installed before disconnecting it.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the AEV 1 Actuator harness connector and the PDC harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity of the (F929) Fused B+ circuit or high resistance connection to ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Is there continuity between ground and the (F929) Fused B+ circuit?</span></div><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (F929) Fused B+ circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (F929) FUSED B+ CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Verify the integrity of the (F929) Fused B+ supply Fuse.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (F929) Fused B+ circuit between the AEV 1 Actuator harness connector and the Power Distribution Center (PDC).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F929) Fused B+ circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE AEV 1 GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between ground and the AEV 1 Actuator Ground circuit at the AEV 1 Actuator harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair AEV 1 Actuator Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>INSPECT THE AEV 1 ACTUATOR WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the AEV 1 Actuator and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           When inspecting wiring and connectors be sure to include inspection of midline connectors in the circuit.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for any loose, or partially broken ground wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the AEV 1 Actuator and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 ACTUATOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the AEV 1 Actuator in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1216 active exhaust valve 1 circuit high\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1216</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 CIRCUIT HIGH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the Active Exhaust Valves are to reduce exhaust noise in order to meet pass-by noise regulations. The Active Exhaust Valves consist of two parts. First is the mechanical butterfly valves that are welded into the exhaust pipe on each bank. Mounted to each of these is a smart actuator. They are connected to the mechanical valves through a transmission spring. This is to help reduce heat from transferring between the mechanical butterfly valves and the actuators.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Active Exhaust Valve actuators communicate with the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) over a LIN Bus circuit. The Active Exhaust Valve actuator 1 (left) and Active Exhaust Valve actuator 2 (right) each has a unique part number/internal ID. The PCM can identify each actuator location by this unique ID. The PCM sends a position command to the Active Exhaust Valve actuators based on engine torque, rpm and vehicle speed. The Active Exhaust Valve actuators move the butterfly valves to the commanded position. An internal Hall Effect sensor counts the pulses and determines valve position. The valve actuators are calibrated at every Key-ON event. The PCM sends full open and full closed commands and checks actual position against commanded position. If for any reason the calibration is unsuccessful, the actuators are self-diagnosing and report fault flags to the PCM over the LIN Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the valve position doesn&#x27;t match a predetermined calibration, a performance code is set and the valves will default to the full open position. If an actuator is not attached to the mechanical valve, or the transmission spring is broken or missing, the actuator will continue to rotate indefinitely and set a fault. Also, if the mechanical valve is stuck and will not move, a fault will set.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           There is a crossover in the exhaust, upstream of the valves that will allow the exhaust to flow through the open valve in the event one of the valves is stuck closed.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the transmission spring breaks or the valve becomes disconnected from the actuator for whatever reason the valve assembly likely will cause a rattling noise with the engine running.</div></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs with the engine running.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator detects that the supply voltage on the Fused B+ (F929) circuit is above 17.5 volts for at least 1 second.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM (OVERCHARGING)</li><li>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 ACTUATOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ANY CHARGING SYSTEM RELATED DTCS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            This code will only set if system voltage is at or above 17.5 volts or the Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator is reporting a false condition.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, check the system voltage.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage at or above 17.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the condition that is causing the overcharge condition, erase DTCs.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 ACTUATOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If all other checks are good.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Replace the Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 1</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1217 active exhaust valve 1 performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1217</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the Active Exhaust Valves are to reduce exhaust noise in order to meet pass-by noise regulations. The Active Exhaust Valves consist of two parts. First is the mechanical butterfly valves that are welded into the exhaust pipe on each bank. Mounted to each of these is a smart actuator. They are connected to the mechanical valves through a transmission spring. This is to help reduce heat from transferring between the mechanical butterfly valves and the actuators.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Active Exhaust Valve actuators communicate with the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) over a LIN Bus circuit. The Active Exhaust Valve actuator 1 (left) and Active Exhaust Valve actuator 2 (right) each has a unique part number/internal ID. The PCM can identify each actuator location by this unique ID. The PCM sends a position command to the Active Exhaust Valve actuators based on engine torque, rpm and vehicle speed. The Active Exhaust Valve actuators move the butterfly valves to the commanded position. An internal Hall Effect sensor counts the pulses and determines valve position. The valve actuators are calibrated at every Key-ON event. The PCM sends full open and full closed commands and checks actual position against commanded position. If for any reason the calibration is unsuccessful, the actuators are self-diagnosing and report fault flags to the PCM over the LIN Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the valve position doesn&#x27;t match a predetermined calibration, a performance code is set and the valves will default to the full open position. If an actuator is not attached to the mechanical valve, or the transmission spring is broken or missing, the actuator will continue to rotate indefinitely and set a fault. Also, if the mechanical valve is stuck and will not move, a fault will set.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          There is a crossover in the exhaust, upstream of the valves that will allow the exhaust to flow through the open valve in the event one of the valves is stuck closed.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the transmission spring breaks or the valve becomes disconnected from the actuator for whatever reason the valve assembly likely will cause a rattling noise with the engine running.</div></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Battery voltage between 10.4 and 15.75 volts. Engine run time greater than 2 minutes. Engine running above 500 rpm. Vehicle speed above 0 mph. Coolant temperature above 83°C (181.4°F). No Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator communication faults. Valve calibration completed.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The actual Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator position does not match the commanded position.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MECHANICAL BUTTERFLY VALVE SEIZED</li><li>TRANSMISSION SPRING BROKEN</li><li>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 ACTUATOR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the When Monitored and Set Conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read and record DTCs and Freeze Frame data on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>INSPECT THE ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 ACTUATOR FOR SIGNS OF PHYSICAL DAMAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Inspect the Active Exhaust Valve 1 Assembly and connector for damage due to road debris. Remove the actuator from the valve assembly, inspect the transmission spring, confirm the butterfly valve and spring are free and functional.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Active Exhaust Valve 1 Assembly or connector damaged or disconnected?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the appropriate repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>INSTALL A NEW ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 1 ACTUATOR AND RETEST FOR DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Install a new Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle for a minimum of two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the When Monitored and Set Conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the poor connections.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1218 active exhaust valve 2 circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1218</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 2 CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the Active Exhaust Valves are to reduce exhaust noise in order to meet pass-by noise regulations. The Active Exhaust Valves consist of two parts. First is the mechanical butterfly valves that are welded into the exhaust pipe on each bank. Mounted to each of these is a smart actuator. They are connected to the mechanical valves through a transmission spring. This is to help reduce heat from transferring between the mechanical butterfly valves and the actuators.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Active Exhaust Valve actuators communicate with the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) over a LIN Bus circuit. The Active Exhaust Valve actuator 1 (left) and Active Exhaust Valve actuator 2 (right) each has a unique part number/internal ID. The PCM can identify each actuator location by this unique ID. The PCM sends a position command to the Active Exhaust Valve actuators based on engine torque, rpm and vehicle speed. The Active Exhaust Valve actuators move the butterfly valves to the commanded position. An internal Hall Effect sensor counts the pulses and determines valve position. The valve actuators are calibrated at every Key-ON event. The PCM sends full open and full closed commands and checks actual position against commanded position. If for any reason the calibration is unsuccessful, the actuators are self-diagnosing and report fault flags to the PCM over the LIN Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the valve position doesn&#x27;t match a predetermined calibration, a performance code is set and the valves will default to the full open position. If an actuator is not attached to the mechanical valve, or the transmission spring is broken or missing, the actuator will continue to rotate indefinitely and set a fault. Also, if the mechanical valve is stuck and will not move, a fault will set.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           There is a crossover in the exhaust, upstream of the valves that will allow the exhaust to flow through the open valve in the event one of the valves is stuck closed.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the transmission spring breaks or the valve becomes disconnected from the actuator for whatever reason the valve assembly likely will cause a rattling noise with the engine running.</div></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs with the engine running.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The LIN communication device in the Active Exhaust Valve 2 Actuator reports an open circuit to the PCM.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. Active Exhaust Valve 2 Actuator defaults to open position.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 2 ACTUATOR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 2 ACTUATOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check connections to Active Exhaust Valve 2 Actuator.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Active Exhaust Valve 2 Actuator and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Replace the Active Exhaust Valve 2 Actuator in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 1</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1219 active exhaust valve 2 circuit low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1219</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 2 CIRCUIT LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the Active Exhaust Valves are to reduce exhaust noise in order to meet pass-by noise regulations. The Active Exhaust Valves consist of two parts. First is the mechanical butterfly valves that are welded into the exhaust pipe on each bank. Mounted to each of these is a smart actuator. They are connected to the mechanical valves through a transmission spring. This is to help reduce heat from transferring between the mechanical butterfly valves and the actuators.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Active Exhaust Valve actuators communicate with the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) over a LIN Bus circuit. The Active Exhaust Valve actuator 1 (left) and Active Exhaust Valve actuator 2 (right) each has a unique part number/internal ID. The PCM can identify each actuator location by this unique ID. The PCM sends a position command to the Active Exhaust Valve actuators based on engine torque, rpm and vehicle speed. The Active Exhaust Valve actuators move the butterfly valves to the commanded position. An internal Hall Effect sensor counts the pulses and determines valve position. The valve actuators are calibrated at every Key-ON event. The PCM sends full open and full closed commands and checks actual position against commanded position. If for any reason the calibration is unsuccessful, the actuators are self-diagnosing and report fault flags to the PCM over the LIN Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the valve position doesn&#x27;t match a predetermined calibration, a performance code is set and the valves will default to the full open position. If an actuator is not attached to the mechanical valve, or the transmission spring is broken or missing, the actuator will continue to rotate indefinitely and set a fault. Also, if the mechanical valve is stuck and will not move, a fault will set.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           There is a crossover in the exhaust, upstream of the valves that will allow the exhaust to flow through the open valve in the event one of the valves is stuck closed.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the transmission spring breaks or the valve becomes disconnected from the actuator for whatever reason the valve assembly likely will cause a rattling noise with the engine running.</div></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs with the engine running.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The PCM detects that the Active Exhaust Valve 2 Fused B+ circuit voltage is below 8.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FUSED B+ CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 2 ACTUATOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Allow the engine to idle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F929) FUSED B+ CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Verify the integrity of the (F929) Fused B+ supply Fuse.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Before continuing to the next step, confirm that the Active Exhaust Valve (AEV) 2 Actuator harness connector was properly installed before disconnecting it.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the AEV 2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (F929) Fused B+ circuit between the AEV 2 Actuator harness connector and the Power Distribution Center (PDC).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (AEV) fused B+ circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE AEV 2 GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the AEV 2 Ground circuit at the AEV 2 Actuator harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the AEV 2 Ground circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the AEV 2 Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>INSPECT THE AEV ACTUATOR WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the AEV 2 Actuator and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           When inspecting wiring and connectors be sure to include inspection of midline connectors in the circuit.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for any loose, or partially broken ground wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the AEV Actuator and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE ACTUATOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Active Exhaust Valve Actuator in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool read DTCs</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p121a active exhaust valve 2 circuit high\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P121A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 2 CIRCUIT HIGH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the Active Exhaust Valves are to reduce exhaust noise in order to meet pass-by noise regulations. The Active Exhaust Valves consist of two parts. First is the mechanical butterfly valves that are welded into the exhaust pipe on each bank. Mounted to each of these is a smart actuator. They are connected to the mechanical valves through a transmission spring. This is to help reduce heat from transferring between the mechanical butterfly valves and the actuators.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Active Exhaust Valve actuators communicate with the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) over a LIN Bus circuit. The Active Exhaust Valve actuator 1 (left) and Active Exhaust Valve actuator 2 (right) each has a unique part number/internal ID. The PCM can identify each actuator location by this unique ID. The PCM sends a position command to the Active Exhaust Valve actuators based on engine torque, rpm and vehicle speed. The Active Exhaust Valve actuators move the butterfly valves to the commanded position. An internal Hall Effect sensor counts the pulses and determines valve position. The valve actuators are calibrated at every Key-ON event. The PCM sends full open and full closed commands and checks actual position against commanded position. If for any reason the calibration is unsuccessful, the actuators are self-diagnosing and report fault flags to the PCM over the LIN Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the valve position doesn&#x27;t match a predetermined calibration, a performance code is set and the valves will default to the full open position. If an actuator is not attached to the mechanical valve, or the transmission spring is broken or missing, the actuator will continue to rotate indefinitely and set a fault. Also, if the mechanical valve is stuck and will not move, a fault will set.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           There is a crossover in the exhaust, upstream of the valves that will allow the exhaust to flow through the open valve in the event one of the valves is stuck closed.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the transmission spring breaks or the valve becomes disconnected from the actuator for whatever reason the valve assembly likely will cause a rattling noise with the engine running.</div></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs with the engine running.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Active Exhaust Valve 2 Actuator detects that the supply voltage on the Fused B+ circuit is above 17.5 volts for at least 1 second.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM (OVERCHARGING)</li><li>ELECTRONIC EXHAUST VALVE 2 ACTUATOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ANY CHARGING SYSTEM RELATED DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>This code will only set if system voltage is at or above 17.5 volts or the Active Exhaust Valve 1 is reporting a false condition.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, check the system voltage.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage at or above 17.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the condition that is causing the overcharge condition, erase DTCs.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE ACTUATOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the AEV 2 Actuator harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the AEV 2 Actuator.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If all other checks are good.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Replace the AEV 2 Actuator in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to the DTC INDEX</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p121b active exhaust valve 2 performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P121B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 2 PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The purpose of the Active Exhaust Valves are to reduce exhaust noise in order to meet pass-by noise regulations. The Active Exhaust Valves consist of two parts. First is the mechanical butterfly valves that are welded into the exhaust pipe on each bank. Mounted to each of these is a smart actuator. They are connected to the mechanical valves through a transmission spring. This is to help reduce heat from transferring between the mechanical butterfly valves and the actuators.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Active Exhaust Valve actuators communicate with the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) over a LIN Bus circuit. The Active Exhaust Valve actuator 1 (left) and Active Exhaust Valve actuator 2 (right) each has a unique part number/internal ID. The PCM can identify each actuator location by this unique ID. The PCM sends a position command to the Active Exhaust Valve actuators based on engine torque, rpm and vehicle speed. The Active Exhaust Valve actuators move the butterfly valves to the commanded position. An internal Hall Effect sensor counts the pulses and determines valve position. The valve actuators are calibrated at every Key-ON event. The PCM sends full open and full closed commands and checks actual position against commanded position. If for any reason the calibration is unsuccessful, the actuators are self-diagnosing and report fault flags to the PCM over the LIN Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the valve position doesn&#x27;t match a predetermined calibration, a performance code is set and the valves will default to the full open position. If an actuator is not attached to the mechanical valve, or the transmission spring is broken or missing, the actuator will continue to rotate indefinitely and set a fault. Also, if the mechanical valve is stuck and will not move, a fault will set.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          There is a crossover in the exhaust, upstream of the valves that will allow the exhaust to flow through the open valve in the event one of the valves is stuck closed.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the transmission spring breaks or the valve becomes disconnected from the actuator for whatever reason the valve assembly likely will cause a rattling noise with the engine running.</div></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Battery voltage between 10.4 and 15.75 volts. Engine run time greater than 2 minutes. Engine running above 500 rpm. Vehicle speed above 0 mph. Coolant temperature above 83°C (181.4°F). No Active Exhaust Valve 2 Actuator communication faults. Valve calibration completed.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The actual Active Exhaust Valve 1 Actuator position does not match the commanded position.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>MECHANICAL BUTTERFLY VALVE SEIZED</li><li>TRANSMISSION SPRING BROKEN</li><li>ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 2 ACTUATOR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the When Monitored and Set Conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read and record DTCs and Freeze Frame data on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>INSPECT THE ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 2 ACTUATOR FOR SIGNS OF PHYSICAL DAMAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Inspect the Active Exhaust Valve 2 Assembly and connector for damage due to road debris. Remove the actuator from the valve assembly, inspect the transmission spring, confirm the butterfly valve and spring are free and functional.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Active Exhaust Valve 2 Assembly or connector damaged or disconnected?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the appropriate repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>INSTALL A NEW ACTIVE EXHAUST VALVE 2 ACTUATOR AND RETEST FOR DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Install a new Active Exhaust Valve 2 Actuator in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle for a minimum of two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the When Monitored and Set Conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the poor connections.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1239 engine oil temperature too low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1239</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ENGINE OIL TEMPERATURE TOO LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Once the Ambient Air Temperature (AAT), Intake Air Temperature (IAT), and Engine Coolant Temperature (ECT) Sensors have been evaluated the Engine Oil Temperature (EOT) Sensor can be checked. If the ambient, engine coolant, and general temperature sensor rationalities indicate valid sensor readings then the engine oil temperature rationality will assume the AAT and ECT Sensors are correct and therefore can be used to evaluate the EOT Sensor.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">To determine failing status, the difference between the starting EOT and starting ECT is compared to a threshold. If the calculated difference is above the threshold, then starting EOT is compared to starting AAT. The diagnostic will check if a block heater is being used to determine if larger threshold values are needed. If this rationality test fails, then it is tested again using the updated value of AAT. A failure here will result in a fault being set for EOT sensor rationality.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the engine running.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Battery voltage greater than 7.5 volts. The model predicted engine oil temperature at engine start is less than 58°C (136.4°F) to initiate the monitor. The monitor will stop when the model predicted engine oil temperature is greater than 88°C (190.4°F).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The actual engine oil temperature is below the model predicted temperature by more than 104°F (40°C) for three minutes.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ENGINE OIL</li><li>COOLING SYSTEM NOT OPERATING TO SPECIFICATION</li><li>HIGH RESISTANCE IN THE EOT SIGNAL CIRCUIT</li><li>HIGH RESISTANCE IN THE SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT</li><li>ENGINE OIL TEMPERATURE SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose any other Engine Oil Temperature Sensor DTCs before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If possible, allow the vehicle to sit with the ignition off in an environment where the temperature will allow the oil temperature to cool down below the engine start model predicted temperature.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to reach normal operating conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ENGINE OIL</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The following conditions must be checked: LOW ENGINE OIL ENGINE MECHANICAL TOLERANCES OUT OF SPECIFICATION ENGINE OIL PRESSURE OUT OF SPECIFICATION ENGINE OIL MEETS OEM SPECIFICATION DETERIORATED OR DIRTY OIL ENGINE OIL CONTAMINATED (i.e., coolant and/or fuel) COOLING SYSTEM NOT OPERATING TO SPECIFICATION</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any of the above conditions found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR HIGH RESISTANCE IN THE (G24) EOT SIGNAL CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Engine Oil Temperature Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">CAUTION:         Do not probe the PCM harness connectors. Probing the PCM harness connectors will damage the PCM terminals resulting in poor terminal to pin connection. Install the GPEC Diagnostic Adaptor to perform the diagnosis.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect the (special tool #10436, Adapter, GPEC Diagnostic).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (G24) Engine Oil Temp Signal circuit between the Engine Oil Temperature Sensor harness connector and the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (G24) Engine Oil Temperature Signal circuit for high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK FOR HIGH RESISTANCE IN THE (K915) SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (K915) Sensor ground circuit between the Engine Oil Temp Sensor harness connector and the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K915) Sensor Ground circuit for high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>ENGINE OIL TEMPERATURE SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Engine Oil Temperature Sensor voltage.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The sensor voltage should be approximately 5.0 volts (plus or minus.1 volts) with the connector disconnected.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect a jumper between the (G24) EOT Signal circuit and the Sensor Ground circuit at the Engine Oil Temperature Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Engine Oil Temperature Sensor voltage.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The sensor voltage should be 0.0 volts (plus or minus.1 volts) with the jumper in place.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display the voltage as described above?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the EOT Sensor and Control Module connectors. Replace the Engine Oil Temperature Sensor if no problems were found with the connectors. Refer to SENSOR, OIL TEMPERATURE, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the Engine Oil Temperature Sensor and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Monitor the scan tool data relative to this circuit and wiggle test the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Look for the data to change or for the DTC to reset during the wiggle test.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1300 crankshaft position learn out of range\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1300</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CRANKSHAFT POSITION LEARN OUT OF RANGE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine start time is greater than 50 seconds. ECT Sensor above 75°C (167°F). A/C off.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">During closed throttle decel event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">One of the CKP Sensor target windows has more than 2% variance from the reference.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TARGET WHEEL/PULSE RING</li><li>WIRE HARNESS</li><li>CRANKSHAFT POSITION SENSOR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>PERFORM THE CAM/CRANK RELEARN PROCEDURE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The Cam/Crank Variation Relearn must be performed anytime there has been a repair/replacement made to a powertrain system, for example: flywheel, valvetrain, camshaft and/or crankshaft sensors or components.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool select the &quot;Cam Crank Relearn&quot; procedure under PCM Miscellaneous Menu Option and follow the on screen instructions.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If a negative response is displayed after the Cam/Crank Relearn procedure is performed, start the engine and perform the Cam/Crank Relearn procedure over until the misfire monitor is cleared.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the PCM complete the Cam/Crank Relearn procedure?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the process over until the Relearn procedure is completed.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on, engine not running.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase all DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair is complete.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>WIRE HARNESS INSPECTION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Visually inspect the CKP wire harness. Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Visually inspect the CKP wire harness connectors. Look for broken, bent, pushed out, or corroded terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Crank Position Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Ensure that the Crankshaft Position Sensor is properly installed and the mounting bolt(s) are torqued to the proper specification.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any of the above conditions present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>TARGET WHEEL/FLEX PLATE INSPECTION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the Crankshaft Position Sensor. Refer to SENSOR, CRANKSHAFT POSITION, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Inspect the Target Wheel/Flex Plate for damage, foreign material, or excessive movement.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair or replace the Target Wheel/Flex Plate as necessary. Refer to CRANKSHAFT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CRANKSHAFT POSITION SENSOR</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If there are no possible causes remaining, view repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Crankshaft Position Sensor. Refer to SENSOR, CRANKSHAFT POSITION, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1400 aftermarket calibration detected/warranty coverage confirmation required\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1400</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">AFTERMARKET CALIBRATION DETECTED/WARRANTY COVERAGE CONFIRMATION REQUIRED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. Battery voltage greater than 10.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) software is unauthorized and does not meet factory OEM specifications. An authorized Mopar or Scat Pak Powertrain Control Module (PCM) has been installed.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This is a non MIL fault.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POSSIBLE CAUSES</li><li>PCM HAS BEEN PROGRAMMED WITH UNAUTHORIZED OR AFTERMARKET SOFTWARE</li><li>AN AUTHORIZED MOPAR OR SCAT PAK POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) HAS BEEN INSTALLED</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">DETERMINE IF THE POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) OR SOFTWARE IS FACTORY AUTHORIZED</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Use information from MOPAR Star Parts or MOPAR Performance/Accessories to help verify if a PCM or software is factory authorized.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the Scan Tool, verify if the PCM or software is factory authorized.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           It is important to use the Scan tool to read the PCM part number and software number, because the part labels may not match the true part number or software in the PCM.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using DealerConnect, verify that the sales codes for the vehicle indicate that correct factory authorized performance parts/kits have been added to the vehicle.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the PCM or software factory authorized?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">No repair is needed.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Inform the Owner of the vehicle that an unauthorized PCM or software is installed. Note information on the repair order.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1456 fuel tank pressure sensor circuit low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1456</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">FUEL TANK PRESSURE SENSOR CIRCUIT LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Fuel Tank Pressure (FTP) Sensor provides the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) with information on vapor pressure inside the fuel tank. The FTP Sensor is a transducer that varies resistance according to changes in pressure. The PCM provides a 5-Volt supply and sensor ground. The sensor sends a feedback voltage to the PCM on the signal circuit. As the fuel tank pressure changes, the feedback voltage changes proportionally.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. Battery voltage greater than 10.38 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Fuel Tank Pressure (FTP) Sensor input voltage is below the minimum acceptable value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POSSIBLE CAUSES</li><li>FTP SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>FTP SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT</li><li>FUEL TANK PRESSURE SENSOR (FTP)</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE FTP SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the FTP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The scan tool should display the P1457-FUEL TANK PRESSURE SENSOR HIGH DTC as active or pending with the connector disconnected.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display as described above?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the FTP Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors. Replace the FTP Sensor if no problems were found with the connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (N7) FTP SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (N7) FTP Signal circuit at the FTP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (N7) FTP Signal circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (N7) FTP Signal circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK FOR THE (N7) FTP SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE (K917) FTP SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (N7) FTP Signal circuit and the (K917) FTP Sensor Ground circuit at the FTP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (N7) FTP Signal circuit and the (K917) FTP Sensor Ground circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the short between the (N7) FTP Signal circuit and the (K917) FTP Sensor Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors for the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1457 fuel tank pressure sensor circuit high\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1457</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">FUEL TANK PRESSURE SENSOR CIRCUIT HIGH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Fuel Tank Pressure (FTP) Sensor provides the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) with information on vapor pressure inside the fuel tank. The FTP Sensor is a transducer that varies resistance according to changes in pressure. The PCM provides a 5-Volt supply and sensor ground. The sensor sends a feedback voltage to the PCM on the signal circuit. As the fuel tank pressure changes, the feedback voltage changes proportionally.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. Battery voltage greater than 10.38 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Fuel Tank Pressure Sensor (FTP) signal voltage is above the maximum voltage threshold.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POSSIBLE CAUSES</li><li>FTP SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>FTP SIGNAL CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>FTP SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT</li><li>SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>FUEL TANK PRESSURE (FTP) SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to reach normal operating temperature.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any system voltage or sensor supply voltage DTCs before continuing with this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (N7) FTP SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the FTP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (N7) FTP Signal circuit at the FTP harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage reading above 5.2 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (N7) FTP Signal circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (N7) FTP SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">CAUTION:        Do not probe the PCM harness connectors. Probing the PCM harness connectors will damage the PCM terminals resulting in poor terminal to pin connection. Install the GPEC Diagnostic Adaptor to perform the diagnosis.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the (special tool #10436, Adapter, GPEC Diagnostic).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (N7) FTP Signal circuit between the FTP harness connector and the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (N7) FTP Signal circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK FOR THE (N7) FTP SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE (K859) 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (N7) FTP Signal circuit and the (K859) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the FTP harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (N7) FTP Signal circuit and the (K859) 5-Volt Supply circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the short between the (N7) FTP Signal circuit and the (K859) 5-Volt Supply circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (K917) FTP SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (K917) Sensor Ground circuit from the FTP harness connector to the appropriate terminal on the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K917) Sensor ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>FTP SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the PCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect a jumper between the (N7) FTP Signal circuit and the (K917) Sensor Ground circuit in the Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, monitor the FTP voltage.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The sensor voltage should be approximately 0.0 volts (plus or minus.1 volt) with the jumper in place.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display the voltage as described above?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the FTP and Powertrain Control Module connectors. Replace the FTP if no problems were found with the connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the FTP Sensor and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the FTP and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p150d cold start rough idle - open throttle start\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P150D</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">COLD START ROUGH IDLE - OPEN THROTTLE START</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Cold start. Engine running at idle only. Ambient Air temperature between -7°C and 50°C (19.4°F and 122°F). Engine Coolant temperature between -7°C and 50°C (19.4°F and 122°F). The difference between the Ambient Air temp and ECT temp at Start is equal to or less than 10°C (50°F).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If a rough idle is detected, the accelerator pedal was depressed during cranking and the Dynamic Crankshaft Fuel Control remains or returns to the high limit window for a calibrated time.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ECT SENSOR, WIRING, OR CONNECTORS</li><li>MAP SENSOR, WIRING, OR CONNECTORS</li><li>FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM</li><li>O2 SENSOR, WIRING, OR CONNECTORS</li><li>ENGINE MECHANICAL SYSTEM</li><li>IGNITION SYSTEM</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>ENGINE COOLANT TEMPERATURE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any other active component or circuit DTCs before continuing with this procedure.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Allow the engine to cool to ambient temperature before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, compare the AAT, ECT and IAT Sensor values.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor value within 15°C (59°F) of the other two sensor values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Review the vehicle repair history for any misfire condition repairs that have been performed. Diagnose and repair any misfire DTCs that are present before continuing with this procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order. Copy DTC and Freeze Frame information to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine and allow it idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Attempt to operate the vehicle under conditions similar to which the DTC was set.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>VISUAL INSPECTION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Anything that affects the speed of the crankshaft can cause this DTC to set.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Inspect the engine for any of the following conditions: Worn serpentine belt Misalignment or binding water pump, P/S pump or A/C Compressor pulleys Improper CKP, CMP, or MAP mounting Poor connector/terminal to component connection for CKP Sensor, CMP Sensor, MAP Sensor, Fuel Injector, Ignition Coil, etc. Vacuum leaks Restriction in the air induction or exhaust system Internal engine component malfunction</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Rough Idle may occur and may not be caused by component failure. Any of the following conditions can be the cause:</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Moisture on ignition system components Insufficient fuel Low quality fuel Manual transmission bog Towing overload</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>MAP SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a scan tool, read the Barometric Pressure.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The Barometric Pressure should be approximately equal to the actual barometric pressure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect a Vacuum Gauge to a Manifold Vacuum source.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Allow the engine to idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If engine will not idle, maintain a constant rpm above idle.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read the MAP Sensor vacuum value.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If necessary, compare the Barometric Pressure value of this vehicle to the value of a known good vehicle of a similar make and model.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the scan tool reading for MAP vacuum within 1 inch of Hg of the Vacuum Gauge and is the Barometric Pressure reading of the vehicle approximately the same as actual Barometric Pressure?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the MAP Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors. Replace the MAP Sensor if no problems were found with the connectors.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECKING THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform the CHECKING THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM test procedure. Refer to CHECKING THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM (HARD START) .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>SPARK PLUG</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the Spark Plugs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect the Spark Plugs and Ignition Coils/Ignition cables for the following conditions: Cracks Carbon Tracking Foreign Material Spark Plug gap size out of specifications Loose or broken electrode Fouling</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Lightly tap the bottom of the spark plug on a solid surface. The electrode in the spark plug should not move.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any of the above conditions present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Spark Plugs. If a Spark Plug was found to have carbon tracking or was fouled, verify that the Ignition Coil is not damaged.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>ENGINE MECHANICAL</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for any of the following conditions/mechanical problems: ENGINE VACUUM - must be at least 13 inches in neutral ENGINE VALVE TIMING - must be within specifications ENGINE COMPRESSION - must be within specifications ENGINE EXHAUST SYSTEM - must be free of any restrictions or leaks. ENGINE PCV SYSTEM - must flow freely TORQUE CONVERTER STALL SPEED - must be within specifications POWER BRAKE BOOSTER - no internal vacuum leaks FUEL - must be free of contamination CYLINDER LEAKAGE TEST - must be within specifications</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any engine mechanical problems?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the related Sensor, Coil, Injector and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the related Sensors, Coils, Injectors and the Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1524 oil pressure out of range - camshaft advance/retard disabled\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1524</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">OIL PRESSURE OUT OF RANGE - CAMSHAFT ADVANCE/RETARD DISABLED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the engine running. Battery voltage above 11.49 volts. Engine speed above 1100 rpm. Oil temperature between 7.0°C (44.6°F) and 188.0°C (370.4°F). No active Engine Oil Temperature Sensor or Engine Oil Pressure Sensor circuit faults.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No active Cam/Crank Misalignment or VCT Solenoid performance faults.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The engine oil pressure never reaches the calibrated specification to allow the VCT activation.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ENGINE OIL/ENGINE MECHANICAL</li><li>ENGINE OIL PRESSURE SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and test drive the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ENGINE OIL/ENGINE MECHANICAL</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             The following items must be considered before determining the cause of this DTC. Failure to do so may lead to misdiagnosis. For the VCT to enable the oil pressure has to be approximately 42 psi. For the VCT to remain enabled the engine oil pressure can not drop below 31 psi. When checking the engine oil pressure use a mechanical gauge.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">LOW ENGINE OIL OIL DIRTY OR DETERIORATED (Lack of scheduled oil changes) CORRECT VISCOSITY ENGINE OIL CONTAMINATED (i.e., coolant and/or fuel) OIL FILTER INSTALLED INCORRECTLY OR DOES NOT MEET OEM SPECIFICATION ENGINE MECHANICAL TOLERANCES OUT OF SPECIFICATION</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Were any of the above conditions present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE ENGINE OIL PRESSURE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the Oil Pressure Sensor and connect an oil pressure gauge to the engine. Refer to SENSOR, OIL PRESSURE, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Start the engine and monitor the oil pressure gauge.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Raise the engine speed while monitoring the oil pressure gauge.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           For the VCT to enable the oil pressure has to be approximately 42 psi. For the VCT to remain enabled the engine oil pressure can not drop below 31 psi. When checking the engine oil pressure use a mechanical gauge.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the engine produce enough oil pressure to enable VCT actuation?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the engine for loss of oil pressure.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>ENGINE OIL PRESSURE SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the Engine Oil Pressure Sensor in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and test drive the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the Engine Oil Pressure Sensor and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1572 brake pedal stuck on\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1572</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BRAKE PEDAL STUCK ON</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. In plant mode only. Battery voltage above 10.4 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) determines that the Brake Pedal input is stuck on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This is a non MIL fault.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CAN BUS FAILURE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose any Communication DTCs before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Ignition on</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           It may be necessary to drive the vehicle to meet the conditions to set this DTC, try to repeat the conditions in which the fault originally set by reviewing the Freeze Frame data.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>BRAKE PEDAL SENSOR CIRCUIT DTCS SET IN THE ABS MODULE</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Are any Brake Pedal Sensor Circuit DTCs set in the ABS module?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Diagnose the appropriate Brake Pedal Sensor DTC in the ABS module. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the Antilock Brake Module (ABS) and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1573 brake pedal stuck off\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1573</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BRAKE PEDAL STUCK OFF</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. In plant mode only. Battery voltage above 10.4 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) determines that the Brake Pedal input is stuck off.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This is a non MIL fault. If P1572 sets, P1573 will also set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CAN BUS FAILURE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Diagnose any Communication DTCs before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Ignition on</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          It may be necessary to drive the vehicle to meet the conditions to set this DTC, try to repeat the conditions in which the fault originally set by reviewing the Freeze Frame data.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>BRAKE SWITCH SENSOR CIRCUIT DTCS SET IN THE ABS MODULE</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Are any Brake Pedal Sensor Circuit DTCs set in the ABS module?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Diagnose the appropriate Brake Switch DTC in the ABS module. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the Antilock Brake Module (ABS) and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1593 speed control switch 1/2 stuck\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1593</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SPEED CONTROL SWITCH 1/2 STUCK</small><small>العطل: عالق (Stuck)</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">THEORY OF OPERATION-SPEED CONTROL SWITCH &amp; SCM (BUSSED)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Speed Control Switch is hard wired to the Steering Control Module (SCM). The SCM includes the steering column shroud, the Steering Angle Sensor (SAS), the Clockspring, the Multi-function Switch, a Steering Column Power Tilt and Telescope Switch (if equipped), and a trim cover. The SCM is located near the top of the steering column below the steering wheel. The speed control and SAS messages are bussed to the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) via the Can Bus.</p></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuously with the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The switch voltage does not register a valid cruise position.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>SPEED CONTROL SWITCH</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Diagnose and repair any Can bus, communication or implausible signal DTCs or Speed Control Switch DTCs in the Steering Control Module (SCM) before proceeding with this test.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Do not place an intact non-deployed airbag face down on a hard surface, the airbag propels into the air if accidentally deployed. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             Visually and physically inspect the wiring harness between the Speed Control Switch harness connector and the SCM harness connector. Repair any damaged wires, connectors, and open/spread terminals. If harness is OK, proceed with test.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Speed Control Switch in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SWITCH, SPEED CONTROL, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1607 pcm internal shutdown timer rationality\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1607</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PCM INTERNAL SHUTDOWN TIMER RATIONALITY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs once per ignition cycle when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Shortly after an initial engine start. The difference between the coolant temperature and ambient air temperature is less than 15°C (59°F) at initial engine start. The engine coolant temperature recorded at the last engine shut down was above 83°C (181.4°F). If the previous engine shut down temperature was not above this value, the shut down diagnostic will not be performed during this ignition cycle. If the above monitoring conditions are met, the PCM uses the engine coolant temperature drop to calculate a minimum ignition off time threshold. It then compares the previous ignition off time to the calibrated minimum threshold.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The PCM determines that the actual previous ignition off time is below the calculated minimum threshold.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">MIL is illuminated</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>COOLING SYSTEM ISSUES</li><li>AMBIENT AIR TEMPERATURE (AAT) SENSOR</li><li>ENGINE COOLANT TEMPERATURE (ECT) SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) SOFTWARE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK THE POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) SOFTWARE LEVEL</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             An aftermarket block heater installed may cause this DTC to set.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, Verify that the PCM is operating at the latest software version available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins or PCM flash updates that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any Service Bulletins or PCM flash updates available for this condition?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the appropriate repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE AAT SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Allow the vehicle to sit with the ignition off in an environment where the temperature is consistent and above -7°C (19.4°F) until the engine coolant temperature is equal, or close to the environmental ambient temperature.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With a scan tool, compare the AAT Sensor value to the current ambient temperature.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the AAT Sensor value within 10°C (18°F) of the current ambient temperature?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>LOW COOLANT LEVEL</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Never open the cooling system when the engine is hot. The system is under pressure. Failure to follow these instructions can result in personal injury including extreme burns, scalding, or fatal injury. Allow the engine to cool before opening the cooling system.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the cooling system to make sure that the coolant is in good condition and at the proper level. Refer to DIAGNOSIS AND TESTING .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the coolant level and condition OK?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Inspect the vehicle for a coolant leak and add the necessary amount of coolant. Refer to TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE COOLING SYSTEM OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If engine coolant temperature is above 65°C (149°F), allow the engine to cool until it is below 65°C (149°F).</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>During engine warm-up monitor the Engine Coolant Temperature degree value. The temperature value change should be a smooth transition from start up to normal operating temp 82°C (180°F). Also monitor the actual coolant temperature with a digital thermometer at or near the ECT Sensor and Thermostat positions.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          As the engine warms up to operating temperature, the actual coolant temperature (thermometer reading) and the scan tool Engine Coolant Temperature degree values should stay relatively close to each other.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Was the digital thermometer readings relatively close to the scan tool reading for the ECT Sensor?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ECT Sensor in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK RELATED PCM AND COMPONENT CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that apply.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Reconnect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1610 supercharger bypass valve position sensor 1 circuit low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1610</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE POSITION SENSOR 1 CIRCUIT LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. Battery voltage greater than 6.98 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The SCB Valve Signal 1 voltage is below 0.45 volts for 0.07 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT SHORTED TO SCB VALVE SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO SCB VALVE SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE ETC MOTOR (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any system voltage or 5-Volt Reference DTCs before continuing with this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F855) 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage between 4.9 to 5.1 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (K871) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (K871) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (K915) SCB VALVE RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit and the (K915) SCB Valve Return circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit and the (K915) SCB Valve Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the short between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit and the (K915) SCB Valve Return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (K871) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (K874) SCB VALVE CONTROL (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit and the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit and the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the short between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit and the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (K871) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">CAUTION:       Do not probe the PCM harness connectors. Probing the PCM harness connectors will damage the PCM terminals resulting in poor terminal to pin connection. Install the GPEC Diagnostic Adaptor to perform the diagnosis.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the (special tool #10436, Adapter, GPEC Diagnostic).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit between the SCB Valve harness connector and the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the excessive resistance in the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>SCB VALVE POSITION SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Reconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect a jumper between the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit and the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The P1611-SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE POSITION SENSOR 1 CIRCUIT HIGH DTC should be active or pending with the jumper in place.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display as described above?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the SCB Valve and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If no problems are found, replace the SCB Valve Assembly. After installation is complete, using a scan tool select the RELEARN function.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the SCB Valve and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the SCB Valve and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1611 supercharger bypass valve position sensor 1 circuit high\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1611</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE POSITION SENSOR 1 CIRCUIT HIGH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. Battery voltage greater than 10.4 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The TPS 1 Signal voltage is above the maximum calibrated threshold.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>SCB VALVE 1 SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE SCB VALVE CONTROL (+) CIRCUIT</li><li>SCB VALVE SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Diagnose and repair any SCB Valve circuit, system voltage or 5-Volt Reference DTCs before continuing with this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (K871) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage reading above 5.2 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (K871) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">CAUTION:        Do not probe the PCM harness connectors. Probing the PCM harness connectors will damage the PCM terminals resulting in poor terminal to pin connection. Install the GPEC Diagnostic Adaptor to perform the diagnosis.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the (special tool #10436, Adapter, GPEC Diagnostic).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit from the SCB Valve harness connector to the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK FOR THE (K871) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE (F855) 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit and the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit in the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit and the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the short between the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit and the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (K915) SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (K915) Sensor Ground circuit from the SCB Valve harness connector to the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K915) Sensor Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>SCB VALVE POSITION SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on, engine not running.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect a jumper between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit and the (K915) SCB Valve Return circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The scan tool should display a P1610-SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE SENSOR 1 CIRCUIT LOW DTC as active or pending with the jumper in place.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display the DTC as described above?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the SCB Valve and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If OK, replace the SCB Valve Assembly. After installation is complete, using a scan tool select the RELEARN function.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the SCB Valve and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the SCB Valve and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1616 supercharger bypass valve position sensor 2 circuit low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1616</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE POSITION SENSOR 2 CIRCUIT LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. Battery voltage greater than 6.98 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">SCB Valve 2 voltage is less than 0.16 volts for 0.7 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE SCB VALVE RETURN CIRCUIT</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE ETC MOTOR (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any system voltage or 5-Volt Reference DTCs before continuing with this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F855) 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage between 4.9 to 5.1 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (K872) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (K872) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (K915) SCB VALVE RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit and the (K915) SCB Valve Return circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit and the (K915) SCB Valve Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the short between the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit and the (K915) SCB Valve Return circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (K872) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (K874) SCB VALVE CONTROL (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit and the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit and the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the short between the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit and the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (K872) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">CAUTION:       Do not probe the PCM harness connectors. Probing the PCM harness connectors will damage the PCM terminals resulting in poor terminal to pin connection. Install the GPEC Diagnostic Adaptor to perform the diagnosis.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the (special tool #10436, Adapter, GPEC Diagnostic).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit between the SCB Valve harness connector and the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the excessive resistance in the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>SCB VALVE POSITION SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Reconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect a jumper between the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit and the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The P1617-SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE POSITION SENSOR 2 CIRCUIT HIGH DTC should be active or pending with the jumper in place.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display as described above?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the SCB Valve and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If no problems are found, replace the SCB Valve Assembly. After installation is complete, using a scan tool select the RELEARN function.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the SCB Valve and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the SCB Valve and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1617 supercharger bypass valve position sensor 2 circuit high\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1617</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE POSITION SENSOR 2 CIRCUIT HIGH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. Battery voltage greater than 6.98 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit voltage is above 4.96 volts for 0.07 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE SCB VALVE CONTROL (+) CIRCUIT</li><li>SCB VALVE SENSOR RETURN CIRCUIT OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Diagnose and repair any SCB Valve circuit, system voltage or 5-Volt Reference DTCs before continuing with this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (K872) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage reading above 5.2 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (K872) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">CAUTION:        Do not probe the PCM harness connectors. Probing the PCM harness connectors will damage the PCM terminals resulting in poor terminal to pin connection. Install the GPEC Diagnostic Adaptor to perform the diagnosis.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the (special tool #10436, Adapter, GPEC Diagnostic).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit from the SCB Valve harness connector to the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK FOR THE (K872) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE (F855) 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit and the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit in the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit and the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the short between the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit and the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (K915) SCB VALVE RETURN CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (K915) SCB Valve Return circuit from the SCB Valve harness connector to the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K915) SCB Valve Return circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>SCB VALVE POSITION SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on, engine not running.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect a jumper between the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit and the (K915) SCB Valve Return circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The scan tool should display a P1616-SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE SENSOR 2 CIRCUIT LOW DTC as active or pending with the jumper in place.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display the DTC as described above?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the SCB Valve and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If OK, replace the SCB Valve Assembly. After installation is complete, using a scan tool select the RELEARN function.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the SCB Valve and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the SCB Valve and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1618 sensor reference voltage 1 erratic\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1618</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SENSOR REFERENCE VOLTAGE 1 ERRATIC</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The 5-Volt Supply circuit voltage is below the minimum acceptable value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. The ETC light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>5-VOLT SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Improperly installed aftermarket accessories can cause this DTC to set. Check for any improperly installed aftermarket accessories before continuing with this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect all the Sensor harness connectors that share the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            This code can be caused by the improper installation of after market accessories that may be causing excessive noise on the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the CKP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (K852) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the APP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the there continuity between ground and the Primary 5-Volt Supply circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Primary 5-Volt Supply circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>SENSOR SHORTED TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the PCM C2 harness connector and all the previously disconnected Sensor harness connectors except for the Throttle Body harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the Throttle Body harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            You must Turn the Ignition off when disconnecting any of the Sensor harness connectors and Turn the Ignition on to check the voltage readings.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>While monitoring the voltage, disconnect each Sensor harness connector that shares the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit, one at a time including the APP Sensor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the voltage increase to above 4.9 volts when disconnecting any of the Sensor harness connectors?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the related Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If OK, replace the Sensor that causes the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit voltage to increase when disconnected.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>5-VOLT SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect all the previously disconnected Sensor harness connectors except for the CKP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the CKP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage between 4.9 and 5.1 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the CKP Sensor and Powertrain Control Module harness connectors. If OK, replace the Crankshaft Position Sensor. Refer to SENSOR, CRANKSHAFT POSITION, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (F855) 5-VOLT SUPPLY FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect all the Sensor harness connectors that share the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (F855) Primary 5-Volt Supply circuit in the CKP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (K852) Primary 5-Volt Supply circuit in the APP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Primary 5-Volt Supply circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (F855) 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance in the (F855) Primary 5-Volt Supply circuit from the Sensor harness connector to the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>It may be necessary to perform this test from every sensor that uses the (F855) Primary 5-Volt Supply circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F855) Primary 5-Volt Supply circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the related Sensors and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the related Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1620 supercharger bypass valve control circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1620</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE CONTROL CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs with the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the error between the actual position and the desired position of the SCB Valve Motor Driver, based on the rate of change, exceeds a calibrated threshold for one second.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. The ETC light will flash.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LOW BATTERY VOLTAGE</li><li>SCB VALVE CONTROL (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>SCB VALVE CONTROL (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>SCB VALVE CONTROL (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO 12 VOLTS</li><li>SCB VALVE CONTROL (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO 12 VOLTS</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE CONTROL</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Low battery voltage can also cause excessive current draw, in very hot and very cold ambient temperatures. Make sure the battery can pass a load test before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (K873) SCB VALVE CONTROL (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">CAUTION:        Do not probe the PCM harness connectors. Probing the PCM harness connectors will damage the PCM terminals resulting in poor terminal to pin connection. Install the GPEC Diagnostic Adaptor to perform the diagnosis.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect the (special tool #10436, Adapter, GPEC Diagnostic).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit from the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector to the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (K874) SCB VALVE CONTROL (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit from the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector to the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK FOR THE SCB VALVE CONTROL CIRCUITS SHORTED TO 12 VOLTS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Reconnect the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the PCM C2 harness connector with the GPEC Adaptor still connected in line.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, actuate the Supercharger Bypass Valve.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit at the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit at the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The voltage reading should change as the valve position is changed. A reading that stays at 12 volts would indicate a short to voltage.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage reading steady at 12 volts for either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit or (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            A short to voltage on the motor circuits can damage the internal H-Bridge driver of the PCM and cause it to be open. After repairing the short to voltage, verify that the PCM was not damaged.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the voltmeter positive lead to the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the voltmeter negative lead to the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, actuate the Supercharger Bypass Valve.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage changing as the SCB Valve position changes?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If a short to voltage as repaired on either of the SCB Valve Control circuits in the previous step, repair is complete. If not, replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the Supercharger Bypass Valve and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Supercharger Bypass Valve and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1621 o2 sensor reference voltage circuit low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1621</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 SENSOR REFERENCE VOLTAGE CIRCUIT LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">O2 Sensor Heater Operation: For a typical Switching (4 Wire) Oxygen (O2) Sensor output signal to function the sense element must be heated to operating temperature. A resistive heater element is incorporated within the sensor to allow for rapid heating of the sensor to reach operating temperature faster and closed loop fuel control. The O2 Sensor Heater resistance is directly proportional to the heater temperature, meaning that as heater temperature increases, the heater resistance increases. The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) makes a calculation to determine the heater resistance and temperature. The heater resistance is calculate by measuring the Battery voltage and current draw on the heater control circuit, Then the heater temperature is determined using the resistance versus temperature characteristic. The heater temperature is monitored continuously and the heating rate is adjusted using Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) to prevent damaging the heating element. If the PCM detects a fault in the O2 Sensor heater circuitry the internal PCM driver is disabled during the current ignition cycle,</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">O2 Sensor Output Operation: Normal range of the O2 Sensor output is a 0 to 1.0 volt Analog to Digital (A/D) signal when the sensor is in normal operating temperature range. The output voltage is generated by comparing the Oxygen content in the atmosphere, collected in a reference chamber to the Oxygen content in the exhaust stream collected in a comparison chamber. When the oxygen content is high (caused by a lean air/fuel mixture) the sensor produces a low voltage. When the oxygen content is low (caused by a rich air/fuel mixture) it produces a higher voltage. In some instances a negative offset output of up to -1.0 volt may be introduced if the sensor&#x27;s reference chamber is contaminated. To allow for the negative voltage to be read, each O2 Sensor Return circuit has a 2.5 volt bias added to shift the signal voltage to between 2.5 volts and 3.5 volts.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">O2 Sensor Diagnostics: The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) performs diagnostics on the heater control, signal and sensor return circuits. Because of how the O2 Sensor operates, the circuit fault diagnostics for O2 Sensors are algorithm based. This means an open or short in one of the O2 Sensor circuits can cause a fault to set against another of the O2 Sensor circuits. Understanding how to interpret the combination of DTCs and O2 Sensor data provided can aid in narrowing down where the fault is in the system.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">On vehicle/engine combinations that use only the traditional switching O2 Sensors, both of the Upstream and Downstream O2 Sensor Return circuits originate from a single source within the PCM. Because of this, a short anywhere in the wiring in any of the O2 Sensor Return circuits will affect all of the Upstream and Downstream O2 Sensors. On vehicle/engine combinations that have wide-band Upstream O2 Sensors and switching Downstream O2 Sensors, the Upstream and Downstream O2 Sensor Return circuits are separate within the PCM. In this case a short anywhere in the wiring in the Downstream O2 Sensor Return circuit(s) will only affect the Downstream O2 Sensor(s). The PCM performs individual diagnostics on the O2 Sensor Return circuit for each wide-band Upstream O2 Sensor.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In data display on the scan tool, filtering on O2 in the search function will bring up the following info:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">O2 Sensor signal voltage - the raw signal voltage should switch between 2.5 and 3.5 volts on a normally functioning sensor. O2 Sensor (0-1) signal voltage - this is the differential signal voltage which is calculated using the raw signal voltage minus the 2.5 volt bias on the return circuit of a normally functioning O2 Sensor. Heater driver operation - displays the heater duty cycle. Heater temperature - this is determined by the total heater circuit resistance. Closed loop fuel control state - displays as open/closed.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Using the Scan Tool for Diagnostics: An open circuit or direct short to voltage or ground will cause the PCM to disable the heater PWM control. The heater will remain disabled for the remainder of that ignition cycle, even if the condition is intermittent and heals itself during that ignition cycle. Any of these conditions should set an O2 Sensor Heater Low or High DTC. Since the heater directly affects the output of sensor signal, and the heater control is disabled, this will cause the affected O2 Sensor raw signal voltage to read high (usually stays above 4.0 volts) and can also eventually set a Signal Circuit High DTC. It is not unusual to have a Heater Control Circuit High or Low DTC and a Sensor Signal High DTC to be set together. Important Note: A small amount of resistance (3-4 Ohms) may not set a Heater Control Circuit DTC but will affect heater operation and cause the sensor signal high DTC to set. Monitoring the heater duty cycle and temperature for a sensor that is reading high on the raw signal voltage can help in diagnosing this issue. A heater circuit with 4.0 - 5.0 Ohms resistance can increase the heater temperature reading on the scan tool for the affected sensor by as much as 700 degrees when compared to the other Switching (4 wire) O2 Sensors. As little as 2.0 Ohms can increase the temperature reading approximately 250 degrees on the scan tool.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE: When a normally operating Switching O2 Sensor is heated to operating temperature the typical duty cycle percentage O2 Sensor Heater Diagnosis:                     will be between approximately 30 and 50 percent. The typical heater temperature will range between approximately 1200°F and 1400°F on the scan tool. If there is an issue with the O2 Sensor heater or circuitry the PCM will disable the heater driver and the duty cycle will be 0 percent. Any issues in the heater</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Using the Scan Tool for Diagnostics: circuitry, even a small amount of resistance, will cause the temperature reading to be noticeably different. Monitoring the scan tool and starting the engine when the O2 Sensor Signal is shorted to ground, and when the O2 Sensor is cold, it will show the raw signal voltage at 0 volts but the (0-1) differential voltage signal will read -2.5 volts and increase toward 0.0 volts as the sensor heats up. When the sensor is warm the raw signal voltage reading and the O2 Sensor Signal Low Diagnosis: (0-1) differential voltage reading will both read near 0.0 volts. It will also pull the sensor return bias voltage low through the O2 Sensor. This will cause the raw voltage signals to switch between the 0 -1 volt range on the other O2 Sensors. This may also cause the O2 Sensor Reference (Return) Voltage Circuit Low DTC to set. The O2 Sensor Signal High diagnostic can fail due to several conditions. As mentioned above, an open, short or any resistance in the heater circuitry can cause the signal voltage to remain high. Looking for abnormalities in the heater duty cycle or heater temperature of the affected sensor would indicate a heater control issue causing the signal circuit O2 Sensor Signal High Diagnosis:               high fault. An open in a sensor return circuit will cause the raw signal voltage to read high, near 5.0 volts, and the (0-1) differential voltage reading to be near 2.5 volts for the affected sensor or sensors. An open in the signal circuit will have the same effect on the sensor. If both Upstream or Downstream O2 Sensors are affected, it could indicate an open in the return circuit that is before the splice in the harness.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1621 o2 sensor reference (return) the o2 sensor reference circuit low/high diagnostic is used to monitor the o2 sensor return circuits. if any of the\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1621</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 Sensor Reference (Return) The O2 Sensor Reference Circuit Low/High diagnostic is used to monitor the O2 Sensor Return circuits. If any of the</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Circuit Low Diagnosis:                         return circuits are shorted to ground the raw signal voltage readings for all O2 Sensors will read between 0-1 volts instead of 2.5-3.5 volts. This will happen because the bias voltage on the return circuit is pulled low for all sensors. As mentioned in the O2 Sensor Signal Low Diagnosis above, a short to ground in one of the sensor signal circuits will also pull the sensor return low for all sensors. However, this will cause the voltage reading on the sensor that has the shorted signal to read 0.0 volts on both the raw signal voltage and (0-1) differential voltage reading when the sensor is warm.</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1622 o2 sensor reference (return) a short to voltage in any of the sensor return circuits will cause the fault to set. the affected o2 sensors will read 5.0\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1622</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 Sensor Reference (Return) A short to voltage in any of the sensor return circuits will cause the fault to set. The affected O2 Sensors will read 5.0</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Circuit High Diagnosis:                        volts on the raw signal voltage. The (0-1) differential voltage reading will be 0.0 volts because the signal circuit voltage and return circuit voltage are both 5.0 volts. A short to voltage on one of the O2 Sensor signal circuits will cause the same fault condition and scan tool readings when the sensor is warm. If the condition is present when the engine is started and the sensor is cold, the (0-1) differential voltage reading will start at 2.5 volts and decrease to 0.0 volts as the sensor warms up.</p></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Battery voltage between 11.0 and 15.75 volts. With the engine running.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Downstream O2 Sensor Return circuit voltage is less than 0.9 - 0.96 volts depending on calibration for approximately 9.0 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR RETURN CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>DOWNSTREAM OXYGEN SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR ANY APPLICABLE SERVICE BULLETINS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins or flash updates that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any Service Bulletins or flash updates available?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the Service Bulletins or flash update.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle long enough for the O2 Sensors to enter closed loop operation (approximately 30 seconds).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR VOLTAGE READINGS ON THE SCAN TOOL</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, select the Data tab and monitor the voltage readings for the Downstream O2 Sensors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the raw voltage readings for the Downstream O2 Sensors to determine if the sensors are switching between 0-1 volt or if one sensor is stuck near 0.0 volts.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Pick the correct scenario below:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Both O2 Sensors are switching between 0-1 volts on the raw O2 Sensor Signal voltage reading</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">One O2 Sensor is reading 0.0 volts and the other O2 Sensor is switching between 0-1 volts on the raw O2 Sensor Signal voltage reading</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">This indicates a short to ground on the signal circuit of the Downstream O2 Sensor reading near 0.0 volts. Repair the O2 Sensor Signal circuit of the O2 Sensor that is reading near 0.0 volts for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK FOR A SHORTED DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan. Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect one of the Downstream O2 Sensor harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, monitor the voltage readings of the Downstream O2 Sensor that is STILL CONNECTED.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the fault is caused by an O2 Sensor that is internally shorted, the other O2 Sensor should change from below one volt to switching between 2.5 - 3.5 volts when the faulty O2 Sensor is disconnected.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Reconnect the O2 Sensor harness connector and repeat this step for each of the Downstream O2 Sensors on the vehicle.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the voltages change to approximately 2.5 - 3.5 volts for the O2 Sensors STILL CONNECTED when disconnecting any one of the sensors?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the faulty O2 Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, OXYGEN, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR RETURN CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the O2 Sensor 1/2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the O2 Sensor 2/2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the Downstream O2 Sensor Return circuit at the O2 Sensor 1/2 or 2/2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the Downstream O2 Sensor Return circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Downstream O2 Sensor Return circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK RELATED PCM AND COMPONENT CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that apply.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Reconnect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The wiring or poor connection problem has been repaired.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1622 o2 sensor reference voltage circuit high\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1622</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 SENSOR REFERENCE VOLTAGE CIRCUIT HIGH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">O2 Sensor Heater Operation: For a typical Switching (4 Wire) Oxygen (O2) Sensor output signal to function the sense element must be heated to operating temperature. A resistive heater element is incorporated within the sensor to allow for rapid heating of the sensor to reach operating temperature faster and closed loop fuel control. The O2 Sensor Heater resistance is directly proportional to the heater temperature, meaning that as heater temperature increases, the heater resistance increases. The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) makes a calculation to determine the heater resistance and temperature. The heater resistance is calculate by measuring the Battery voltage and current draw on the heater control circuit, Then the heater temperature is determined using the resistance versus temperature characteristic. The heater temperature is monitored continuously and the heating rate is adjusted using Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) to prevent damaging the heating element. If the PCM detects a fault in the O2 Sensor heater circuitry the internal PCM driver is disabled during the current ignition cycle,</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">O2 Sensor Output Operation: Normal range of the O2 Sensor output is a 0 to 1.0 volt Analog to Digital (A/D) signal when the sensor is in normal operating temperature range. The output voltage is generated by comparing the Oxygen content in the atmosphere, collected in a reference chamber to the Oxygen content in the exhaust stream collected in a comparison chamber. When the oxygen content is high (caused by a lean air/fuel mixture) the sensor produces a low voltage. When the oxygen content is low (caused by a rich air/fuel mixture) it produces a higher voltage. In some instances a negative offset output of up to -1.0 volt may be introduced if the sensor&#x27;s reference chamber is contaminated. To allow for the negative voltage to be read, each O2 Sensor Return circuit has a 2.5 volt bias added to shift the signal voltage to between 2.5 volts and 3.5 volts.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">O2 Sensor Diagnostics: The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) performs diagnostics on the heater control, signal and sensor return circuits. Because of how the O2 Sensor operates, the circuit fault diagnostics for O2 Sensors are algorithm based. This means an open or short in one of the O2 Sensor circuits can cause a fault to set against another of the O2 Sensor circuits. Understanding how to interpret the combination of DTCs and O2 Sensor data provided can aid in narrowing down where the fault is in the system.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">On vehicle/engine combinations that use only the traditional switching O2 Sensors, both of the Upstream and Downstream O2 Sensor Return circuits originate from a single source within the PCM. Because of this, a short anywhere in the wiring in any of the O2 Sensor Return circuits will affect all of the Upstream and Downstream O2 Sensors. On vehicle/engine combinations that have wide-band Upstream O2 Sensors and switching Downstream O2 Sensors, the Upstream and Downstream O2 Sensor Return circuits are separate within the PCM. In this case a short anywhere in the wiring in the Downstream O2 Sensor Return circuit(s) will only affect the Downstream O2 Sensor(s). The PCM performs individual diagnostics on the O2 Sensor Return circuit for each wide-band Upstream O2 Sensor.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In data display on the scan tool, filtering on O2 in the search function will bring up the following info:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">O2 Sensor signal voltage - the raw signal voltage should switch between 2.5 and 3.5 volts on a normally functioning sensor. O2 Sensor (0-1) signal voltage - this is the differential signal voltage which is calculated using the raw signal voltage minus the 2.5 volt bias on the return circuit of a normally functioning O2 Sensor. Heater driver operation - displays the heater duty cycle. Heater temperature - this is determined by the total heater circuit resistance. Closed loop fuel control state - displays as open/closed.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Using the Scan Tool for Diagnostics: An open circuit or direct short to voltage or ground will cause the PCM to disable the heater PWM control. The heater will remain disabled for the remainder of that ignition cycle, even if the condition is intermittent and heals itself during that ignition cycle. Any of these conditions should set an O2 Sensor Heater Low or High DTC. Since the heater directly affects the output of sensor signal, and the heater control is disabled, this will cause the affected O2 Sensor raw signal voltage to read high (usually stays above 4.0 volts) and can also eventually set a Signal Circuit High DTC. It is not unusual to have a Heater Control Circuit High or Low DTC and a Sensor Signal High DTC to be set together. Important Note: A small amount of resistance (3-4 Ohms) may not set a Heater Control Circuit DTC but will affect heater operation and cause the sensor signal high DTC to set. Monitoring the heater duty cycle and temperature for a sensor that is reading high on the raw signal voltage can help in diagnosing this issue. A heater circuit with 4.0 - 5.0 Ohms resistance can increase the heater temperature reading on the scan tool for the affected sensor by as much as 700 degrees when compared to the other Switching (4 wire) O2 Sensors. As little as 2.0 Ohms can increase the temperature reading approximately 250 degrees on the scan tool.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE: When a normally operating Switching O2 Sensor is heated to operating temperature the typical duty cycle percentage O2 Sensor Heater Diagnosis:                     will be between approximately 30 and 50 percent. The typical heater temperature will range between approximately 1200°F and 1400°F on the scan tool. If there is an issue with the O2 Sensor heater or circuitry the PCM will disable the heater driver and the duty cycle will be 0 percent. Any issues in the heater</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Using the Scan Tool for Diagnostics: circuitry, even a small amount of resistance, will cause the temperature reading to be noticeably different. Monitoring the scan tool and starting the engine when the O2 Sensor Signal is shorted to ground, and when the O2 Sensor is cold, it will show the raw signal voltage at 0 volts but the (0-1) differential voltage signal will read -2.5 volts and increase toward 0.0 volts as the sensor heats up. When the sensor is warm the raw signal voltage reading and the O2 Sensor Signal Low Diagnosis: (0-1) differential voltage reading will both read near 0.0 volts. It will also pull the sensor return bias voltage low through the O2 Sensor. This will cause the raw voltage signals to switch between the 0 -1 volt range on the other O2 Sensors. This may also cause the O2 Sensor Reference (Return) Voltage Circuit Low DTC to set. The O2 Sensor Signal High diagnostic can fail due to several conditions. As mentioned above, an open, short or any resistance in the heater circuitry can cause the signal voltage to remain high. Looking for abnormalities in the heater duty cycle or heater temperature of the affected sensor would indicate a heater control issue causing the signal circuit O2 Sensor Signal High Diagnosis:               high fault. An open in a sensor return circuit will cause the raw signal voltage to read high, near 5.0 volts, and the (0-1) differential voltage reading to be near 2.5 volts for the affected sensor or sensors. An open in the signal circuit will have the same effect on the sensor. If both Upstream or Downstream O2 Sensors are affected, it could indicate an open in the return circuit that is before the splice in the harness.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1621 o2 sensor reference (return) the o2 sensor reference circuit low/high diagnostic is used to monitor the o2 sensor return circuits. if any of the\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1621</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 Sensor Reference (Return) The O2 Sensor Reference Circuit Low/High diagnostic is used to monitor the O2 Sensor Return circuits. If any of the</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Circuit Low Diagnosis:                         return circuits are shorted to ground the raw signal voltage readings for all O2 Sensors will read between 0-1 volts instead of 2.5-3.5 volts. This will happen because the bias voltage on the return circuit is pulled low for all sensors. As mentioned in the O2 Sensor Signal Low Diagnosis above, a short to ground in one of the sensor signal circuits will also pull the sensor return low for all sensors. However, this will cause the voltage reading on the sensor that has the shorted signal to read 0.0 volts on both the raw signal voltage and (0-1) differential voltage reading when the sensor is warm.</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1622 o2 sensor reference (return) a short to voltage in any of the sensor return circuits will cause the fault to set. the affected o2 sensors will read 5.0\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1622</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">O2 Sensor Reference (Return) A short to voltage in any of the sensor return circuits will cause the fault to set. The affected O2 Sensors will read 5.0</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Circuit High Diagnosis:                        volts on the raw signal voltage. The (0-1) differential voltage reading will be 0.0 volts because the signal circuit voltage and return circuit voltage are both 5.0 volts. A short to voltage on one of the O2 Sensor signal circuits will cause the same fault condition and scan tool readings when the sensor is warm. If the condition is present when the engine is started and the sensor is cold, the (0-1) differential voltage reading will start at 2.5 volts and decrease to 0.0 volts as the sensor warms up.</p></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Battery voltage between 11.0 - 15.75 volts. With the engine running.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Downstream O2 Sensor Return circuit voltage is above approximately 3.7 volts for 9.0 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR RETURN CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>DOWNSTREAM OXYGEN SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR ANY APPLICABLE SERVICE BULLETINS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins or flash updates that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any Service Bulletins or flash updates available?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the Service Bulletins or flash update.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR VOLTAGE READINGS ON THE SCAN TOOL</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on, engine not running.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool select the Data tab and monitor all of the O2 Sensor raw voltage readings.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not use the O2 volts (0-1) data.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle long enough for the O2 Sensors to enter closed loop operation (approximately 30 seconds).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The O2 Sensor voltages should normally be switching between approximately 2.5 - 3.5 volts with the engine idling. If an O2 Sensor signal or reference circuit is shorted to voltage, the voltage readings will read approximately 5.0 volts.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are both O2 Sensor voltage readings switching between approximately 2.5 - 3.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR A SHORTED DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan. Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect either of the Downstream O2 Sensor harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, monitor the voltage readings of the Downstream O2 Sensor that is STILL CONNECTED.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the fault is caused by an O2 Sensor that is internally shorted or the signal circuit shorted to voltage, the other O2 Sensor should change to switching between 2.5 - 3.5 volts when the faulty O2 Sensor is disconnected.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Reconnect the O2 Sensor harness connector and repeat this step for the other Downstream O2 Sensor on the vehicle.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the voltage change to approximately 2.5 - 3.5 volts for the O2 Sensor STILL CONNECTED when disconnecting either of the sensors?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE FAULTY DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Downstream O2 Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage on the O2 Sensor Signal circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage above 5.0 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the O2 Sensor Signal circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the faulty O2 Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, OXYGEN, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR (K904) RETURN CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the O2 Sensor 1/2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the O2 Sensor 2/2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage on the Downstream O2 Sensor (K904) Return circuit at the O2 Sensor 1/2 or 2/2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage above 2.75 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Downstream O2 Sensor (K904) Return circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK RELATED PCM AND COMPONENT CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that apply.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Reconnect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The wiring or poor connection problem has been repaired.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1627 supercharger bypass valve position sensor 1/2 correlation\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1627</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE POSITION SENSOR 1/2 CORRELATION</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the engine running. No Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve Position Sensor or MAP Sensor DTCs present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) recognizes that the SCB Valve Position Sensor 1 and 2 are not coherent.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ETC light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>HIGH RESISTANCE IN THE SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 OR SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT</li><li>HIGH RESISTANCE IN THE 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT</li><li>HIGH RESISTANCE IN THE SCB VALVE RETURN CIRCUIT</li><li>SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If there are any SCB Valve Position Sensor 1 or 2 circuit faults present, diagnose and repair those faults before proceeding with this test procedure.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the SCB Valve plate is at the idle position and free from binding and carbon build up.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT DTC diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR HIGH RESISTANCE IN THE (K871) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">CAUTION:         Do not probe the PCM harness connectors. Probing the PCM harness connectors will damage the PCM terminals resulting in poor terminal to pin connection. Install the GPEC Diagnostic Adaptor to perform the diagnosis.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector and connect the (special tool #10436, Adapter, GPEC Diagnostic) in-line with the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a voltmeter, perform a voltage drop test. Back probe connect the voltmeter between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector and the GPEC Adaptor. Make sure the voltmeter leads are connected so a positive polarity is displayed on the voltmeter.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Monitor the voltmeter.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 0.2 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the excessive resistance in the (K871) TPS 1 Signal circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR HIGH RESISTANCE IN THE (K915) SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Move the voltmeter leads to the (K915) Sensor Ground circuit between the SCB Valve harness connector and the GPEC Adaptor. Make sure the voltmeter leads are connected so a positive polarity is displayed on the voltmeter.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Monitor the voltmeter.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 0.2 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the excessive resistance in the (K915) Sensor Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK FOR HIGH RESISTANCE IN THE (K872) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Move the voltmeter leads between the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector and the GPEC Adaptor. Make sure the voltmeter leads are connected so a positive polarity is displayed on the voltmeter.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Monitor the voltmeter.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 0.2 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the excessive resistance in the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK FOR HIGH RESISTANCE IN THE (F855) 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Move the voltmeter leads between the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the SCB Valve harness connector and the GPEC Adaptor. Make sure the voltmeter leads are connected so a positive polarity is displayed on the voltmeter.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Monitor the voltmeter.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 0.2 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the excessive resistance in the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK FOR A SHORT BETWEEN THE (K871) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 1 CIRCUIT AND THE (K872) SCB VALVE SIGNAL 2 CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for continuity between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit and the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (K871) SCB Valve Signal 1 circuit and the (K872) SCB Valve Signal 2 circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the excessive resistance in the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>REPLACE THE SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE AND RETEST FOR DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and test drive the vehicle. Perform several acceleration and deceleration cycles.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replacing the Supercharger Bypass Valve repaired the fault.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The wiring or poor connection problem has been repaired.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1628 sensor reference voltage 2 erratic\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1628</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SENSOR REFERENCE VOLTAGE 2 ERRATIC</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The 5-Volt Supply circuit voltage is below the minimum acceptable value.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. The ETC light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>5-VOLT SENSOR</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Improperly installed aftermarket accessories can cause this DTC to set. Check for any improperly installed aftermarket accessories before continuing with this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F856) AUXILIARY 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C1 and C2 harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect all the Sensors that share the (F856) Auxiliary 5-Volt Supply circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the APP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Disconnect the Fuel Tank Pressure Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (F856) 5-Volt Supply circuit at a MAP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (K854) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the APP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (K859) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the Fuel Tank Pressure Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and any 5-Volt Supply circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the 5-Volt Supply circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>SENSOR SHORTED TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the PCM C2 harness connector and all the previously disconnected Sensors except for the MAP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (F856) 5-Volt Supply circuit in the MAP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           You must Turn the Ignition off when disconnecting any of the Sensor harness connectors and Turn the Ignition On to check the voltage readings.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>While monitoring the voltage, disconnect each Sensor harness connector that shares the (F856) 5-Volt Supply circuit, one at a time including the APP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the voltage increase above 4.9 volts when disconnecting any of the Sensor harness connectors?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the related Sensor and Powertrain Control Module harness connectors. If no problems are found, replace the Sensor that causes the (F856) 5-Volt Supply circuit voltage to increase when disconnected.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>5-VOLT SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect all the previously disconnected Sensors except for the MAP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (F856) 5-Volt Supply circuit in the MAP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 4.9 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the MAP Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If no problems are found, replace the MAP Sensor. Refer to SENSOR, TMAP-INTAKE MANIFOLD, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (F856) 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C1 and C2 harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect all the Sensors that share the (F856) 5-Volt Supply circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the APP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (F856) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the MAP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (K854) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the APP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (K859) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the Fuel Tank Pressure Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the 5-Volt Supply circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (F856) 5-VOLT SUPPLY CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN/HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance on the Secondary 5-Volt Supply circuits between the Sensor harness connectors and the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>It may be necessary to perform this test from every sensor that uses the 5-Volt Supply circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the 5-Volt Supply circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the related Sensors and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the related Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p162a supercharger bypass valve actuator control system - max pwm exceeded\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P162A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE ACTUATOR CONTROL SYSTEM - MAX PWM EXCEEDED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs with the engine running.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) detects that the Supercharger Bypass Valve duty cycle is over 75% for more than five seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. The ETC light will illuminate. If the PWM stays above 75%, P162B will set first at 1.2 seconds, and P162A will follow at 5 seconds. Root cause is common for both faults</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>COKING OR DEBRIS BLOCKING THE SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE PLATE</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE PLATE BINDING INSIDE THE BORE</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any other DTCs set in the PCM before proceeding with this test.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           An intermittent loss of power to the PCM without performing a Supercharger Bypass Valve Relearn procedure may cause this DTC to set.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Verify that the PCM is at the latest calibration (flash) level. If necessary, update the PCM in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and test drive the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE INSPECTION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the Throttle Body and use a bore scope camera or small mirror to view the Supercharger Bypass Valve.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect for any signs of coking or a foreign material (ice or dirt) on the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate or in the bore causing the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate to stick. Turn the ignition on and use the scan tool to actuate the Supercharger Bypass Valve and check for any sticking.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any signs of foreign material or scoring of the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate or bore found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Clean the throttle blade and bore if possible or replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve in accordance with the Service Information if necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and test drive the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the Supercharger Bypass Valve and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Refer to any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p162b supercharger bypass valve actuator control system - temporary pwm/rpm max exceeded\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P162B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE ACTUATOR CONTROL SYSTEM - TEMPORARY PWM/RPM MAX EXCEEDED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs with the engine running.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) detects that the Supercharger Bypass Valve duty cycle is over 75% for more than 1.2 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. The ETC light will flash. If the PWM stays above 75%, P162B will set first at 1.2 seconds, and P162A will follow at 5 seconds. Root cause is common for both faults.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INTERMITTENT LOSS OF CONNECTION AT THE SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE HARNESS CONNECTOR</li><li>COKING OR DEBRIS BLOCKING THE SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE PLATE</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE PLATE BINDING INSIDE THE BORE</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Diagnose and repair any other DTCs set in the PCM before proceeding with this test.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          An intermittent loss of power to the PCM without performing a Supercharger Bypass Valve Relearn procedure may cause this DTC to set.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Verify that the PCM is at the latest calibration (flash) level. If necessary, update the PCM in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and test drive the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE INSPECTION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the Throttle Body and use a bore scope camera or small mirror to view the Supercharger Bypass Valve.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect for any signs of coking or a foreign material (ice or dirt) on the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate or in the bore causing the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate to stick. Turn the ignition on and use the scan tool to actuate the Supercharger Bypass Valve and check for any sticking.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any signs of foreign material or scoring of the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate or bore found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Clean the throttle blade and bore if possible or replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve in accordance with the Service Information if necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE CONNECTOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the connector for any corroded, pushed out, spread or damaged terminals that can cause an intermittent connection.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           An intermittent loss of a signal from one of the sensors may cause this DTC to set without setting a sensor fault.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and test drive the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the Supercharger Bypass Valve and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Refer to any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p162c supercharger bypass valve control circuit\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P162C</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE CONTROL CIRCUIT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. The Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve Motor not in Limp Home mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) detects a short in the SCB Valve Motor Driver circuit for 0.18 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. The ETC light will flash.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LOW BATTERY VOLTAGE</li><li>SCB VALVE CONTROL (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO 5.0 VOLTS</li><li>SCB VALVE CONTROL (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO 5.0 VOLTS</li><li>SCB VALVE CONTROL (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>SCB VALVE CONTROL (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>SCB VALVE CONTROL (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE SCB VALVE CONTROL (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Low battery voltage can also cause excessive current draw, in very hot and very cold ambient temperatures. Make sure the battery can pass a load test before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (K873) SCB VALVE CONTROL (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO 5.0 VOLTS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for continuity between the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit and the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit and the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit for a short to the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (K874) SCB VALVE CONTROL (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO 5.0 VOLTS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit and (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit at the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit and the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit for a short to the (F855) 5-Volt Supply circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK FOR THE (K873) SCB VALVE CONTROL (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE (K874) SCB VALVE CONTROL (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit and the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit at the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit and the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the short to between the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit and the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (K873) SCB VALVE CONTROL (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit at the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (K874) SCB VALVE CONTROL (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit at the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Reconnect the SCB Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">CAUTION:        Do not probe the PCM harness connectors. Probing the PCM harness connectors will damage the PCM terminals resulting in poor terminal to pin connection. Install the GPEC Diagnostic Adaptor to perform the diagnosis.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #10436, Adapter, GPEC Diagnostic) in-line with the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Reconnect the PCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect the voltmeter positive lead to the (K873) SCB Valve Control (+) circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the voltmeter negative lead to the (K874) SCB Valve Control (-) circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, actuate the Supercharger Bypass Valve.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage changing as the SCB Valve position changes?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors between the Supercharger Bypass Valve and the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals. Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the Supercharger Bypass Valve and Powertrain Control Module connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1643 supercharger bypass valve actuator control system - stuck closed\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1643</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE ACTUATOR CONTROL SYSTEM - STUCK CLOSED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. The air charge temperature is above -10°C (14°F). Supercharger Bypass Valve Self Learn procedure completed.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) detects that the Supercharger Bypass Valve is not in the correct position when checked during the closing spring return test for 0.5 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. The ETC light will flash.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>COKING OR BLOCKAGE OF THE SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE PLATE</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any other Supercharger Bypass Valve DTCs before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The PCM tests the Supercharger Bypass Valve by opening and closing the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate before starting the engine.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE INSPECTION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the Throttle Body and use a bore scope camera or small mirror to view the Supercharger Bypass Valve.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect for any signs of coking or a foreign material (ice or dirt) on the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate or in the bore causing the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate to stick. Turn the ignition on and use the scan tool to actuate the Supercharger Bypass Valve and check for any sticking.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any signs of foreign material or scoring of the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate or bore found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Clean the throttle blade and bore if possible or replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve in accordance with the Service Information if necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the connector for any corroded, pushed out, spread or damaged terminals that can cause an intermittent connection.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1645 supercharger bypass valve actuator control system - unable to close\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1645</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE ACTUATOR CONTROL SYSTEM - UNABLE TO CLOSE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. The air charge temperature is above -10°C (14°F). Supercharger Bypass Valve Self Learn procedure completed.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) detects that the Supercharger Bypass Valve is not in the correct position when checked during the opening spring return test for 0.6 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. The ETC light will flash.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>COKING OR BLOCKAGE OF THE THROTTLE PLATE</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any Supercharger Bypass Valve DTCs before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The PCM tests the Supercharger Bypass Valve by opening and closing the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate before starting the engine.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE INSPECTION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the Throttle Body and use a bore scope camera or small mirror to view the Supercharger Bypass Valve.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect for any signs of coking or a foreign material (ice or dirt) on the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate or in the bore causing the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate to stick. Turn the ignition on and use the scan tool to actuate the Supercharger Bypass Valve and check for any sticking.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any signs of foreign material or scoring of the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate or bore found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Clean the throttle blade and bore if possible or replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve in accordance with the Service Information if necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the connector for any corroded, pushed out, spread or damaged terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1665 supercharger bypass valve control system - ice blockage\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1665</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE CONTROL SYSTEM - ICE BLOCKAGE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Supercharger boost pressure is managed by the use of a Supercharger Bypass (SCB) Valve. The PCM can vary the position of the SCB Valve to control the amount of boost. The SCB system uses two Position Sensors to monitor the SCB blade position. Position Sensors are located within the SCB Valve assembly. Each sensor has its own Signal circuit. Both sensors share a 5-Volt reference circuit (Supply) and a low reference circuit (Sensor Return). The Powertrain Control Module (PCM) monitors the SCB Valve Sensor data. Each Signal circuit provides the PCM with a signal voltage proportional to SCB blade movement. The PCM monitors the data to verify that the indicated SCB position is correct.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. The air charge temperature is below -10°C (14°F). Supercharger Bypass Valve Self Learn procedure completed.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the spring check fails and air charge temperature below -10°C (14°F), the PCM will attempt to break any ice present by slamming the Supercharger Bypass Valve blade open and closed. If this operation fails, P1665 will set.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate. The ETC light will flash.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>COKING OR BLOCKAGE OF THE SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE PLATE</li><li>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any Supercharger Bypass Valve DTCs before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The PCM tests the Supercharger Bypass Valve by opening and closing the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate before starting the engine.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE INSPECTION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the Throttle Body and use a bore scope camera or small mirror to view the Supercharger Bypass Valve.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect for any signs of coking or a foreign material (ice or dirt) on the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate or in the bore causing the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate to stick. Turn the ignition on and use the scan tool to actuate the Supercharger Bypass Valve and check for any sticking.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any signs of foreign material or scoring of the Supercharger Bypass Valve plate or bore found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Clean the throttle blade and bore if possible or replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve in accordance with the Service Information if necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE SUPERCHARGER BYPASS VALVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Supercharger Bypass Valve harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the connector for any corroded, pushed out, spread or damaged terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Supercharger Bypass Valve Assembly in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1696 eeprom memory write denied/invalid\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1696</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">EEPROM MEMORY WRITE DENIED/INVALID</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">An attempt to program/write to the internal EEPROM failed, Also checks at power down.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) SOFTWARE UPDATE</li><li>EXCESSIVE RESISTANCE IN THE PCM POWER OR GROUND CIRCUITS</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Diagnose and repair any other DTCs set in the PCM before proceeding with this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to reach operating temperature.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts, or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions can result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            It may be necessary to test drive the vehicle in order for this DTC to set.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>PCM ODOMETER MILEAGE NOT PROGRAMMED</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Cycle the ignition off, then on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, attempt to perform the Program PCM Odometer function.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Allow the engine to reach normal operating temperature.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The SRI mileage has been successfully programmed into the PCM. Test is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECKING THE PCM POWER AND GROUND CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform the LOST COMMUNICATION WITH THE PCM test procedure. Refer to NO RESPONSE FROM PCM (POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE) .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, attempt to perform the Program PCM Odometer function under the PCM/ECM REPROGRAMMING Procedure. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), MODULE PROGRAMMING . .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Allow the engine to reach normal operating temperature.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The SRI mileage has been successfully programmed into the PCM. Test is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1697 emr (sri) mileage not stored\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1697</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">EMR (SRI) MILEAGE NOT STORED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Odometer mileage has not been programmed into the PCM.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PCM ODOMETER MILEAGE NOT PROGRAMMED</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">PCM ODOMETER MILEAGE NOT PROGRAMMED</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If a PCM has later calibration available, program the PCM in accordance with the Service Information. and follow the PCM/ECM PROGRAMMING procedure. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), MODULE PROGRAMMING .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Allow the engine to reach normal operating temperature.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The SRI mileage has been successfully programmed into the PCM. Test is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1718 eeprom integrity failure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1718</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">EEPROM INTEGRITY FAILURE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">An attempt to program/write to the internal EEPROM failed, Also checks at power down.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) SOFTWARE UPDATE</li><li>EXCESSIVE RESISTANCE IN THE PCM POWER OR GROUND CIRCUITS</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             Diagnose and repair any other DTCs set in the PCM before proceeding with this test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to reach operating temperature.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           It may be necessary to test drive the vehicle in order for this DTC to set.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>PCM ODOMETER MILEAGE NOT PROGRAMMED</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Cycle the ignition off, then on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, attempt to perform the Program PCM Odometer function.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Allow the engine to reach normal operating temperature.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The SRI mileage has been successfully programmed into the PCM. Test is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECKING THE PCM POWER AND GROUND CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform the LOST COMMUNICATION WITH THE PCM test procedure. Refer to NO RESPONSE FROM PCM (POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE) .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, attempt to perform the Program PCM Odometer function.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Allow the engine to reach normal operating temperature.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The SRI mileage has been successfully programmed into the PCM. Test is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1c4e fault in abs/esp module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1C4E</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">FAULT IN ABS/ESP MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. Battery voltage greater than 10.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">An active DTC is stored in the ABS/ESP Module.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DTC PRESENT IN THE ABS MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">DTC PRESENT IN ANTI-LOCK BRAKE MODULE</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>This is an informational DTC to inform you that a DTCs is stored in the Anti-Lock Brake Module.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Erase this DTC after all ABS DTCs have been repaired.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a scan tool, read the Anti-Lock Brake DTC. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">PCM Diagnostic Information complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Continue</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test Complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1cf3 battery temperature sensor out of range low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1CF3</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY TEMPERATURE SENSOR OUT OF RANGE LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Intelligent Battery Sensor (IBS) is an electrical shunt with a microprocessor that is mounted in-line with the negative Battery Cable. The IBS monitors the current flow and voltage. The IBS also has a built in thermistor that calculates the Battery temperature. The microprocessor uses this data to calculate Battery state of charge, Battery internal resistance, charge received, charge delivered, and time in service. This information is reported through a LIN Bus circuit to the Body Control Module (BCM). The BCM broadcasts the information to the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) over the CAN Bus.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Powertrain Control Module uses feedback from the IBS to monitor the Battery temperature under two different conditions: The first condition is at ignition on after a cold soak The second condition checks for an implausible change in temperature</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Condition one: The battery temperature is compared to the Engine Coolant Temperature (ECT) Sensor signal at key on after a cold soak. If the battery temperature is below the ECT temperature by a calibrated threshold, then the battery temperature is compared to the Ambient Air Temperature (AAT) Sensor in the same manner. If this comparison also fails, then an IBS battery temperature failure shall be determined. Condition two: If the change in temperature change is larger than a calibrated threshold within a calibrated period of time, then an IBS battery temperature failure shall be determined.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INTELLIGENT BATTERY SENSOR</li><li>LOST COMMUNICATION WITH BODY CONTROL MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             Diagnose any Communication DTCs before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           It may be necessary to drive the vehicle to meet the conditions to set this DTC, try to repeat the conditions in which the fault originally set by reviewing the Freeze Frame data.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>INTELLIGENT BATTERY SENSOR CIRCUIT DTCS SET IN THE BODY CONTROL MODULE</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Are any Intelligent Battery Sensor Circuit DTCs set in the Body Control Module?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Diagnose the appropriate Intelligent Battery Sensor Circuit DTC in the Body Control Module. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>VERIFY CORRECT BATTERY INSTALLED</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify that the correct battery is installed in the vehicle.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the correct battery installed?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Intelligent Battery Sensor (IBS) in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Battery. Refer to BATTERY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1cf4 battery temperature sensor out of range high\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1CF4</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY TEMPERATURE SENSOR OUT OF RANGE HIGH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Intelligent Battery Sensor (IBS) is an electrical shunt with a microprocessor that is mounted in-line with the negative Battery Cable. The IBS monitors the current flow and voltage. The IBS also has a built in thermistor that calculates the Battery temperature. The microprocessor uses this data to calculate Battery state of charge, Battery internal resistance, charge received, charge delivered, and time in service. This information is reported through a LIN Bus circuit to the Body Control Module (BCM). The BCM broadcasts the information to the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) over the CAN Bus.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Powertrain Control Module uses feedback from the IBS to monitor the Battery temperature under two different conditions: The first condition is at ignition on after a cold soak The second condition checks for an implausible change in temperature.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Condition one: The battery temperature is compared to the Engine Coolant Temperature (ECT) Sensor signal at key on after a cold soak. If the battery temperature is above the ECT temperature by a calibrated threshold, then the battery temperature is compared to the Ambient Air Temperature (AAT) Sensor in the same manner. If this comparison also fails, then an IBS battery temperature failure shall be determined. Condition two: If the change in temperature change is larger than a calibrated threshold within a calibrated period of time, then an IBS battery temperature failure shall be determined.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INTELLIGENT BATTERY SENSOR</li><li>LOST COMMUNICATION WITH BODY CONTROL MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             Diagnose and repair any ECT or AAT Sensor DTCs that may be present before continuing with this test procedure.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             Diagnose and repair any BCM, LIN BUS, communication or IBS DTCs that may be present before continuing with this test procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Intelligent Battery Sensor in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1e09 closed loop fueling not achieved - bank 1 downstream\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1E09</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CLOSED LOOP FUELING NOT ACHIEVED - BANK 1 DOWNSTREAM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With engine running Engine speed between 1100 rpm and 4000 rpm The Upstream O2 Sensor in closed loop mode</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A condition exists where the Downstream O2 Sensor has remained in open loop fuel control, from a start-up condition, longer than a calibrated amount of time, when conditions would have otherwise expected closed loop operation.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POSSIBLE CAUSES</li><li>FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM</li><li>MAP SENSOR, WIRING, OR CONNECTORS</li><li>DOWNSTREAM O2 SENSOR, WIRING, OR CONNECTORS</li><li>ENGINE MECHANICAL SYSTEM</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>READ AND RECORD DTCS AND ENVIRONMENTAL DATA - ERASE DTCS AND CHECK FOR THE DTC TO RETURN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in all Electronic Control Units (ECUs) and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>For future reference, with the scan tool, run and save a vehicle Scan Report and all related recorded data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase all DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition off for a minimum of 10.0 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Using the When Monitored and Set Conditions above and recorded data, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR OTHER DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Refer to the recorded DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any Downstream O2 Sensor or MAP Sensor performance or circuit DTCs active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the applicable diagnostic procedure(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE O2 SENSOR HEATER OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Wait a minimum of 10 minutes to allow the O2 Sensor to cool down before continuing the test. Allow the O2 Sensor voltage to stabilize at 5.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, actuate the O2 Sensor 1/1 Heater Test.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, monitor O2 Sensor 1/1 voltage for at least two minutes.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the voltage stay above 4.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the O2 Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If no problems are found, replace the O2 Sensor.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE O2 SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, monitor the O2 Sensor 1/2 reading.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage switching between 2.5 and 3.4 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Check the O2 Sensor terminals for pushed out, corroded or spread terminals and verify that the wires for the O2 Sensor are not open or shorted to ground. If no problems are found, replace the O2 Sensor.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>MAP SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect a Vacuum Gauge to a Manifold Vacuum source.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Allow the engine to idle.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If engine will not idle, maintain a constant rpm above idle.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the MAP Sensor vacuum value.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the scan tool reading within one inch of Hg as compared to the Vacuum Gauge reading?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify that there is good pin to terminal contact in the MAP Sensor and Powertrain Control Module connectors. If OK, replace the MAP Sensor.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform the CHECKING THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM test procedure. Refer to CHECKING THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM (HARD START) .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK THE ENGINE MECHANICAL SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for any of the following conditions/mechanical problems: AIR INDUCTION SYSTEM - must be free from leaks. ENGINE VACUUM - must be at least 13 inches in park/neutral ENGINE VALVE TIMING - must be within specifications ENGINE COMPRESSION - must be within specifications ENGINE EXHAUST SYSTEM - must be free of any restrictions or leaks. ENGINE PCV SYSTEM - must flow freely TORQUE CONVERTER STALL SPEED - must be within specifications POWER BRAKE BOOSTER - no internal vacuum leaks FUEL - must be free of contamination FUEL INJECTOR - plugged or restricted injector; control wire not connected to correct injector</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any engine mechanical problems?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all PCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all PCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The wiring or poor connection problem has been repaired.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1e0a closed loop fueling not achieved - bank 2 downstream\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1E0A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CLOSED LOOP FUELING NOT ACHIEVED - BANK 2 DOWNSTREAM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With engine running Engine speed between 1100 rpm and 4000 rpm The Upstream O2 Sensor in closed loop mode</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A condition exists where the Downstream O2 Sensor has remained in open loop fuel control, from a start-up condition, longer than a calibrated amount of time, when conditions would have otherwise expected closed loop operation.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The MIL light will illuminate.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POSSIBLE CAUSES</li><li>FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM</li><li>ECT SENSOR, WIRING, OR CONNECTORS</li><li>MAP SENSOR, WIRING, OR CONNECTORS</li><li>O2 SENSOR, WIRING, OR CONNECTORS</li><li>ENGINE MECHANICAL SYSTEM</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING</li><li>PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Diagnose and repair any ECT Sensor, MAP Sensor, or O2 Sensor DTCs before continuing with this procedure.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order. Copy Freeze Frame information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to reach operating temperature.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        When the engine is operating, do not stand in direct line with the fan. Do not put your hands near the pulleys, belts or fan.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Do not wear loose clothing. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle under conditions similar to which the DTC was set.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or pending?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the INTERMITTENT CONDITION diagnostic procedure. Refer to INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform the CHECKING THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM test procedure. Refer to CHECKING THE FUEL DELIVERY SYSTEM (HARD START) .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE ENGINE COOLANT TEMPERATURE SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ECT Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the terminals in the connector for corrosion, spread, broken or partially pushed out terminals that can cause an intermittent connection.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE MAP SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the MAP Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the terminals in the connector for corrosion, spread, broken or partially pushed out terminals that can cause an intermittent connection.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE OXYGEN SENSOR OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the O2 Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the terminals in the connector for corrosion, spread, broken or partially pushed out terminals that can cause an intermittent connection.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE ENGINE MECHANICAL SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for any of the following conditions/mechanical problems: AIR INDUCTION SYSTEM - must be free from leaks. ENGINE VACUUM - must be at least 13 inches in park/neutral ENGINE VALVE TIMING - must be within specifications ENGINE COMPRESSION - must be within specifications ENGINE EXHAUST SYSTEM - must be free of any restrictions or leaks. ENGINE PCV SYSTEM - must flow freely TORQUE CONVERTER STALL SPEED - must be within specifications POWER BRAKE BOOSTER - no internal vacuum leaks FUEL - must be free of contamination FUEL INJECTOR - plugged or restricted injector; control wire not connected to correct injector</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any engine mechanical problems?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors relative to the components tested in this procedure.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Monitor the scan tool data relative to the components tested in this procedure and wiggle test the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for any chafed, pierced, pinched or partially broken wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for broken, bent, pushed out or corroded terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Perform any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910390</p></div></div></details></div></details></div>";
